/* 124 original applied cases. Source references locate topics; no official-exam calibration. */
const COVERAGE_INVESTMENT_CURRENT=[{"id":"b249","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-1.1","reading":"IM-1","concept":"Bad-state factor premium","question":"Two diversified assets have identical expected cash flows. Asset A pays least when investor consumption is lowest; B pays most in those same bad states. Which pricing conclusion is most consistent with a positive price of consumption risk?","choices":["A should have a higher price because its payoff is procyclical.","Both prices must be equal because expected cash flows match.","B must have a higher expected return because it hedges consumption risk.","A should have a lower price and higher expected return."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les paiements de B assurent les mauvais états et ont donc plus de valeur marginale. A exige une prime pour son exposition aux états défavorables.","why":["Un paiement procyclique est moins utile en récession.","La covariance avec l’utilité marginale compte aussi.","La couverture tend à réduire le rendement exigé.","A rémunère le risque non diversifiable de mauvais état."],"cue":"Une prime rémunère un mauvais état, pas toute volatilité.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b250","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-1.2","reading":"IM-1","concept":"CAPM required return","question":"Under the single-period CAPM, the risk-free rate is 3%, the expected market return is 9% and a stock has beta 1.4. Its required expected return is closest to:","choices":["12.6%","15.6%","11.4%","8.4%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Prime de marché=9−3=6 %. Rendement requis=3+1,4×6=11,4 %.","why":["Applique beta au rendement total du marché.","Applique beta au rendement total de marché, puis ajoute rf, au lieu d’utiliser la prime de marché.","Ajoute le taux sans risque à la prime systématique.","Omet le taux sans risque."],"cue":"CAPM : rf + beta × prime de marché.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"3+1.4*(9-3)","value":11.4,"optionValue":11.4,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b251","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-1.3","reading":"IM-1","concept":"Diversified beta exposure","question":"A fully diversified pension equity portfolio has substantial positive market beta. The CIO proposes eliminating its required risk premium by doubling the number of stocks without changing beta. Under CAPM, what is the strongest objection?","choices":["A fully diversified portfolio must have zero expected excess return.","Diversification removes idiosyncratic risk, while the unchanged beta still requires systematic compensation.","Every additional stock reduces beta by the reciprocal of portfolio size.","CAPM prices total volatility even in a fully diversified portfolio."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La diversification réduit le résiduel propre aux titres. Elle ne supprime pas une exposition commune au marché conservée par hypothèse.","why":["Le portefeuille de marché est diversifié et a une prime.","Sépare risque diversifiable et risque de marché.","Beta dépend des covariances et des poids.","Le CAPM rémunère beta, pas tout le risque total."],"cue":"Diversifié ne signifie pas sans risque systématique.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b252","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-1.4","reading":"IM-1","concept":"Multifactor omitted exposure","question":"A market-neutral fund loads positively on a priced liquidity factor. Its average excess return is positive. Which comparison is most defensible?","choices":["A multifactor benchmark can attribute part of the return to liquidity exposure that a market-only CAPM may label alpha.","Zero market beta guarantees zero sensitivity to every other factor.","Adding factors must increase estimated alpha.","The liquidity loading is idiosyncratic merely because market beta is zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un facteur omis rémunéré peut apparaître dans l’intercept d’un modèle incomplet. Ajouter le bon facteur distingue exposition et sélection.","why":["Corrige un benchmark de risque incomplet.","Une neutralité est relative au facteur ciblé.","L’alpha peut augmenter ou diminuer selon les facteurs.","Un risque commun ne devient pas spécifique au titre."],"cue":"Un alpha dépend des risques inclus dans le benchmark.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b253","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-1.5","reading":"IM-1","concept":"Discount factor state valuation","question":"An asset pays 120 in a good state and 80 in a bad state, each with probability 0.5. The stochastic discount factor is 0.8 in the good state and 1.2 in the bad state. Its price is:","choices":["100","104","200","96"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Prix=E[mX]=0,5×0,8×120+0,5×1,2×80=96. Multiplier les deux espérances efface leur covariance négative.","why":["Utilise E[m]E[X], en ignorant la covariance.","Inverse la relation entre paiement et facteur.","Additionne les paiements sans probabilités.","Pondère le produit dans chaque état."],"cue":"Valoriser E[mX], pas E[m]E[X].","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"0.5*0.8*120+0.5*1.2*80","value":96,"optionValue":96,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b254","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-1.6","reading":"IM-1","concept":"Efficient markets and costs","question":"A published accounting signal predicts a gross return spread of 0.6% annually, but implementing it costs 0.9% and exposes investors to a priced distress factor. What follows?","choices":["Transaction costs are irrelevant to market efficiency.","A public signal must have zero correlation with future realized returns.","The gross spread alone does not establish an exploitable risk-adjusted violation of efficiency.","Any predictable gross return proves a costless arbitrage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Il faut isoler prime de risque et gain net réalisable. Une prévisibilité brute ne suffit pas à démontrer une opportunité nette anormale.","why":["Les coûts limitent l’exploitation d’un signal.","Une prime conditionnelle peut être prévisible.","Exige un test tenant compte des risques et coûts.","Prévisibilité et arbitrage ne sont pas synonymes."],"cue":"Tester le rendement net ajusté du risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b255","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-2.1","reading":"IM-2","concept":"Value investing and distress","question":"A value manager buys firms with low price-to-book ratios. An investment committee calls their higher historical average returns proof of investor irrationality. Which qualification is strongest?","choices":["Value investing requires buying the firms with the fastest recent price growth.","The premium may compensate for exposure to adverse economic states; mispricing is an alternative explanation, not established by the average alone.","Low price-to-book firms cannot be financially distressed.","A higher historical return rules out any risk-based explanation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Des rendements moyens élevés peuvent rémunérer un risque économique ou refléter une correction de prix. L’historique seul ne tranche pas.","why":["Cela décrit plutôt une logique de momentum.","Laisse ouvertes les explications rationnelles et comportementales.","Un multiple faible peut refléter des difficultés réelles.","Risque élevé peut précisément expliquer le rendement."],"cue":"Un multiple faible ne prouve pas une erreur de prix.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b256","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-2.2","reading":"IM-2","concept":"Inflation sensitivity of real claims","question":"An unhedged portfolio holds long nominal bonds and shares of a manufacturer unable to pass higher input costs to customers. An unexpected persistent inflation shock occurs, with real yields unchanged. Which first-order combination is most plausible?","choices":["Nominal bond prices fall and the manufacturer’s margins compress.","Nominal bond prices rise and margins expand automatically.","Both exposures are inflation hedges by definition.","Only the bond coupon changes immediately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"L’inflation inattendue augmente le rendement nominal exigé à taux réel inchangé. L’absence de pricing power comprime les marges de l’entreprise.","why":["Suit séparément actualisation et résultat opérationnel.","Inverse les deux mécanismes supposés.","Des créances nominales ne protègent pas automatiquement.","Un coupon fixe ne se réinitialise pas avec l’inflation."],"cue":"Inflation : actualisation et capacité de répercussion.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b257","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-2.3","reading":"IM-2","concept":"Volatility targeting feedback","question":"A fund scales equity exposure inversely with estimated volatility. During a sell-off, its volatility estimate doubles overnight. With the same volatility target and ignoring constraints, what is the main implementation risk?","choices":["Required exposure doubles, necessarily stabilizing the market.","The strategy never trades when prices fall.","Volatility targeting removes transaction costs and gap risk.","Required exposure is halved, potentially forcing sales into a falling market."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une règle d’exposition proportionnelle à 1/vol impose de réduire de moitié le risque pris. Des ventes synchronisées peuvent amplifier la baisse.","why":["Inverse la relation exposition-volatilité.","La volatilité peut déclencher des ventes pendant la baisse.","La règle ne supprime ni friction ni mouvement discontinu.","Identifie la procyclicité de la règle."],"cue":"Une cible de vol peut imposer de vendre en crise.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b258","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-2.4","reading":"IM-2","concept":"Conditional factor beta","question":"A portfolio’s value-factor beta rises from 0.2 in expansions to 0.9 in recessions. A constant-beta Fama–French regression is used for stress testing. Which change best addresses the stated weakness?","choices":["Replace every beta with zero in recessions.","Treat the unconditional alpha as a guarantee for each regime.","Allow factor exposures to depend on economic state and test the conditional specification out of sample.","Delete the value factor because its beta is unstable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un beta moyen masque l’exposition accrue en récession. Un modèle conditionnel doit rendre explicite cette dépendance sans supposer sa stabilité future.","why":["Zéro contredit les données de récession.","Un intercept moyen ne garantit aucun rendement de régime.","Représente la variation documentée des sensibilités.","Supprimer le facteur omettrait un risque observé."],"cue":"Un beta moyen peut masquer le mauvais état.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b259","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-2.5","reading":"IM-2","concept":"Momentum reversal exposure","question":"A manager compares value and momentum. A long-short momentum portfolio has just profited during a prolonged bear market. Which scenario most directly challenges extrapolating that performance?","choices":["Momentum has no exposure to crowded rebalancing.","A sharp market rebound can hurt the short leg of recent losers and produce a momentum crash.","A market rebound necessarily rewards every momentum portfolio.","Value and momentum are identical because both use past stock prices."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Après une baisse, les perdants vendus à découvert peuvent fortement rebondir. La stratégie momentum présente ainsi un risque de retournement marqué.","why":["Des signaux similaires peuvent créer des transactions communes.","Relie la composition du portefeuille au scénario de retournement.","Le signe des positions compte.","Value utilise les prix relatifs aux fondamentaux."],"cue":"Les perdants vendus peuvent rebondir violemment.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b260","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.1","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Leverage constraints and low risk","question":"Investors constrained from borrowing seek high-beta stocks to obtain higher expected returns. Which equilibrium pressure can help explain a low-risk anomaly?","choices":["Demand can bid up high-beta prices, lowering their subsequent risk-adjusted returns.","Borrowing constraints force all investors into zero-beta assets.","Higher prices mechanically guarantee higher future returns.","Low-beta stocks cannot be used in a leveraged portfolio."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La recherche de beta par des investisseurs contraints peut rendre les titres à beta élevé chers. Un faible rendement ultérieur ajusté du risque devient cohérent avec cette pression.","why":["Décrit un mécanisme de survalorisation relative.","Le comportement décrit vise précisément du beta élevé.","Un prix d’entrée plus haut tend à réduire le rendement futur.","Un investisseur non contraint peut les leverager."],"cue":"Contraintes de levier → demande de beta cher.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b261","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.2","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Active return and information ratio","question":"A fund earns 10%, its benchmark earns 7%, the risk-free rate is 2%, tracking error is 4% and total volatility is 16%. Its information ratio, using arithmetic annual active return, is:","choices":["0.50","1.25","2.00","0.75"],"answer":3,"explanation":"IR=(10−7)/4=0,75. Le numérateur est le rendement actif et le dénominateur le tracking error.","why":["C’est le Sharpe (10−2)/16.","Mélange une prime différente et le mauvais calcul.","Utilise la prime sans risque au dénominateur actif.","Utilise les deux grandeurs relatives au benchmark."],"cue":"IR = rendement actif / tracking error.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"(10-7)/4","value":0.75,"optionValue":0.75,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b262","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.3","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Benchmark investability","question":"A small-cap value manager claims superior alpha against a large-cap growth index selected after seeing performance. Which replacement benchmark is most appropriate?","choices":["A noninvestable index with the largest possible constituent count.","A cash benchmark because every equity strategy can be compared only with cash.","An investable small-cap value benchmark specified before evaluation and consistent with the mandate.","The lowest-returning index found after evaluation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le benchmark doit représenter le mandat, être utilisable et ne pas être choisi pour embellir le résultat. Sinon l’écart capte surtout le style.","why":["La taille ne remplace pas la représentativité.","Le cash ignore les risques actions assumés.","Réduit le biais de style et de sélection a posteriori.","Maximise artificiellement l’alpha affiché."],"cue":"Choisir le benchmark avant de voir le résultat.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b263","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.4","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Independent breadth","question":"A manager has information coefficient 0.05 and 100 independent bets per year. Under the unconstrained fundamental law, the maximum information ratio is:","choices":["0.005","0.50","5.00","0.05"],"answer":1,"explanation":"IR≈IC×√BR=0,05×√100=0,50. La racine porte sur les paris indépendants, pas sur les transactions brutes.","why":["Divise au lieu de multiplier par la racine.","Applique la racine au breadth.","Multiplie IC par BR sans racine.","Ignore le nombre de paris."],"cue":"Le breadth mesure des paris indépendants.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"0.05*Math.sqrt(100)","value":0.5,"optionValue":0.5,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b264","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.5","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Factor benchmark expected return","question":"A portfolio has monthly factor loadings 0.8 on market and 0.4 on value. The month’s factor excess returns are 2% and −1%. Its realized excess return is 1.5%. With the factor benchmark intercept set to zero, residual return is:","choices":["0.3%","1.2%","1.5%","−0.3%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Rendement expliqué=0,8×2+0,4×(−1)=1,2 %. Résiduel réalisé=1,5−1,2=0,3 %. Ce résiduel mensuel n’établit pas un alpha statistique.","why":["Soustrait le rendement factoriel du réalisé.","Donne le rendement expliqué, pas le résiduel.","Ignore les facteurs.","Inverse le signe du résiduel."],"cue":"Résiduel réalisé = réalisé − benchmark factoriel.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"1.5-(0.8*2+0.4*(-1))","value":0.3,"optionValue":0.3,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b265","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.6","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Rolling style analysis","question":"A balanced fund shifts materially toward equities over two years. A single full-sample style regression assigns one fixed equity weight. Which diagnostic is most useful?","choices":["Interpret the fixed full-sample weight as the exact allocation in every month.","Discard all benchmark returns because holdings change.","Infer style solely from the fund name.","Estimate constrained rolling or state-dependent style exposures and compare them with the mandate."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une analyse glissante peut révéler la dérive de style masquée par une moyenne sur toute la période. Les contraintes doivent rester cohérentes avec les instruments autorisés.","why":["Un coefficient moyen n’est pas une allocation datée.","Les indices restent informatifs sur les expositions.","Le nom commercial ne mesure aucune sensibilité.","Suit la variation temporelle visée par la question."],"cue":"Une moyenne temporelle peut cacher une dérive.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b266","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.7","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Nonlinear alpha of option selling","question":"A strategy repeatedly sells out-of-the-money puts and shows positive alpha in a linear equity regression during calm years. What is the most important qualification?","choices":["A longer calm sample eliminates crash exposure.","Using total rather than excess returns always removes the bias.","The intercept may reflect compensation for nonlinear downside exposure omitted by the linear benchmark.","Positive linear alpha proves that put writing has no systematic risk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La vente de puts concentre le risque dans la queue basse. Une régression linéaire peut attribuer à tort cette prime optionnelle à la compétence.","why":["L’absence de krach observé ne supprime pas son risque.","Changer le niveau des rendements n’ajoute pas de convexité.","Recherche le risque non linéaire omis.","L’exposition au krach reste économique."],"cue":"Un alpha linéaire peut cacher une vente d’assurance.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b267","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.8","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Beta anomaly versus volatility anomaly","question":"Stock A has low total volatility but high beta relative to the market; stock B has high idiosyncratic volatility but low beta. Which sorting procedure specifically tests the beta anomaly rather than the total-volatility anomaly?","choices":["Exclude the market return when estimating beta.","Sort on estimated market beta while separately controlling total and idiosyncratic volatility.","Sort only on total volatility and call the bottom group low beta.","Treat beta and total volatility as algebraically identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Beta mesure une covariance normalisée, la volatilité mesure la dispersion totale. Les deux tris peuvent donc produire des portefeuilles différents.","why":["Le facteur marché est nécessaire pour estimer beta.","Isole la variable dont l’anomalie est testée.","Le classement par volatilité ne garantit pas celui par beta.","Le risque spécifique rompt cette identité supposée."],"cue":"Faible beta et faible volatilité ne sont pas équivalents.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b268","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-3.9","reading":"IM-3","concept":"Delegated mandates and risk anomaly","question":"A benchmarked manager cannot borrow and is rewarded for outperforming a rising equity index. Which incentive can contribute to expensive high-beta stocks?","choices":["Buying high-beta stocks supplies implicit leverage within the long-only constraint.","Holding only cash always maximizes benchmark-relative return in a rising market.","The mandate prevents any exposure above benchmark beta.","Benchmarking ensures every price equals fundamental value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Acheter davantage de beta permet de rechercher du levier économique sans emprunt explicite. Des incitations communes peuvent soutenir ces prix.","why":["Relie contrainte d’emprunt et demande de titres risqués.","Le cash sous-performe généralement une hausse actions.","Le poids des titres peut accroître beta.","Un contrat de gestion ne garantit pas l’efficience des prix."],"cue":"Les mandats peuvent créer du levier implicite.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b269","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.1","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Uncertain optimizer inputs","question":"An unconstrained mean-variance optimizer assigns almost all capital to two securities after very small changes in estimated expected returns. What is the most appropriate interpretation?","choices":["The concentration proves that the two securities have certain positive alpha.","Covariance information has no role in optimization.","Increasing the number of decimal places in the forecasts solves estimation error.","Estimation error in expected returns can dominate optimized weights, warranting robust estimates and sensible constraints."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un optimiseur transforme les écarts estimés en positions parfois extrêmes. Il faut tenir compte de l’incertitude des entrées et de la stabilité des poids.","why":["Un poids optimal conditionnel ne prouve aucune certitude.","La matrice de covariance reste une entrée essentielle.","La précision d’affichage n’améliore pas l’information.","Identifie la sensibilité à l’erreur d’estimation."],"cue":"Les poids sont aussi fragiles que les prévisions.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b270","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-4.2","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Alpha shrinkage implementation","question":"A research model predicts 8% alpha for an illiquid stock, but similar signals historically realize only half their forecast. Which refinement best uses the evidence before portfolio construction?","choices":["Keep 8% unchanged solely because it came from a model.","Set every stock forecast to the same positive alpha regardless of evidence.","Shrink the raw forecast toward a justified prior and account for forecast uncertainty.","Double the forecast because extreme signals deserve more conviction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le signal brut peut être trop extrême. Une calibration fondée sur les réalisations passées réduit le risque de traduire une erreur en poids excessif.","why":["L’origine quantitative ne garantit pas la fiabilité.","Détruit la discrimination utile entre titres.","Exploite le degré de réalisation observé sans garantir le futur.","Amplifie le défaut de calibration."],"cue":"Calibrer l’alpha avant de l’optimiser.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b271","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.3","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Industry alpha neutralization","question":"An alpha model ranks technology stocks above utilities because of a common sector effect. A manager wants stock selection that is neutral within each sector. Which adjustment best implements that objective?","choices":["Set all sector exposures equal to the portfolio’s historical beta.","Subtract each sector’s cross-sectional mean alpha from the alphas of stocks in that sector.","Subtract the same market-wide constant from every alpha.","Increase technology alphas to preserve their raw advantage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le centrage à l’intérieur de chaque secteur retire la composante sectorielle moyenne et conserve les écarts relatifs entre titres.","why":["Confond neutralité sectorielle et beta de marché.","Neutralise le niveau sectoriel du signal.","Ne retire pas l’écart moyen entre secteurs.","Renforce précisément l’effet à retirer."],"cue":"Neutraliser au niveau du risque que l’on vise.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b272","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.4","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Net alpha after round-trip cost","question":"A proposed position has expected gross alpha of 1.2% over its holding period. Entry costs are 0.5% and expected exit costs 0.8%, each measured against invested capital. Ignore all other effects. Expected net alpha is:","choices":["−0.1%","0.7%","0.4%","2.5%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Alpha net=1,2−0,5−0,8=−0,1 %. Les deux côtés de la transaction réduisent le gain espéré.","why":["Déduit entrée et sortie.","Omet la sortie.","Omet l’entrée.","Ajoute les coûts au rendement."],"cue":"Comparer l’alpha à tous les coûts du cycle.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"1.2-0.5-0.8","value":-0.1,"optionValue":-0.1,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b273","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.5","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Incomplete alpha coverage","question":"A portfolio optimizer has forecasts for 70% of benchmark stocks. The remaining 30% are assigned zero alpha and treated as strong sell signals. What is the principal modeling error?","choices":["Zero alpha always proves that a stock should have zero portfolio weight.","Uncovered stocks have zero covariance with covered stocks.","Risk aversion is irrelevant whenever coverage is incomplete.","A missing forecast is being interpreted as negative evidence relative to covered names rather than uncertainty or a neutral prior."],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’absence d’analyse ne signifie pas une opinion défavorable. Le traitement doit éviter un pari systématique sur la couverture de recherche.","why":["Un titre sans alpha peut servir le benchmark ou la diversification.","La couverture analyste ne détermine pas la covariance.","L’aversion au risque reste nécessaire.","Distingue information manquante et information négative."],"cue":"Pas de prévision ≠ signal de vente.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b274","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.6","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Rebalancing horizon tradeoff","question":"An alpha signal decays slowly over several months, while one-way market impact has doubled. Risk exposures remain within mandate. Which response is most defensible?","choices":["Stop all rebalancing permanently regardless of future risk.","Ignore the cost change because the signal is statistically significant.","Re-evaluate trading urgency and potentially rebalance more gradually if saved costs exceed lost alpha and extra risk.","Trade the full position immediately because any delay always destroys all alpha."],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’urgence dépend du compromis entre décroissance du signal, risque temporaire et coût d’exécution. Un alpha lent donne parfois plus de flexibilité.","why":["Le futur peut justifier de nouvelles transactions.","Une significativité ne paie pas les coûts.","Compare les quatre éléments au même horizon.","La décroissance est lente par hypothèse."],"cue":"L’urgence dépend de la demi-vie du signal.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b275","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.7","reading":"IM-4","concept":"No-trade band with proportional cost","question":"A one-period allocation problem has net objective U(x)=−0.5(x−0.60)^2−0.05|x−x0|, where x0=0.58 is the current risky weight. Ignore constraints. Is trading optimal?","choices":["No: because transaction costs imply that every current allocation is optimal.","No: the marginal benefit at x0 is 0.02, below the marginal trading cost 0.05.","Yes: increase x fully to 0.60 because costs never change the optimum.","Yes: reduce x because the current weight is above target."],"answer":1,"explanation":"À x0, le gain marginal d’une hausse est 0,60−0,58=0,02, inférieur au coût marginal 0,05. Le point courant est dans la bande sans transaction.","why":["Seules certaines déviations sont assez petites.","Applique la condition locale de bande.","Un coût proportionnel crée un seuil.","Le poids courant est inférieur à la cible."],"cue":"Ne pas trader si le gain marginal reste sous le coût.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b276","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.8","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Quadratic portfolio constraints","question":"A manager wants to maximize forecast alpha minus a penalty on portfolio variance while imposing linear position limits. Which technique represents this problem most directly?","choices":["Quadratic programming using the covariance matrix.","A pure screen that ignores covariance and interaction effects.","Linear programming without any reformulation of the variance penalty.","Ranking solely by historical raw returns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La variance est une forme quadratique des poids; les limites de positions sont des contraintes linéaires. La programmation quadratique représente ce compromis.","why":["Représente directement objectif et contraintes.","Un filtre ne gère pas le compromis de covariance complet.","La pénalité de variance n’est pas linéaire.","Le classement ne résout pas l’allocation sous contraintes."],"cue":"Variance quadratique → optimisation quadratique.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b277","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-4.9","reading":"IM-4","concept":"Client account dispersion","question":"Two client accounts follow the same model portfolio but one has legacy tax constraints and receives a large mid-month cash inflow. Their returns diverge. What is the best initial investigation?","choices":["Treat any dispersion as proof that one account’s reported return is fraudulent.","Require identical trades without considering client restrictions.","Ignore dispersion because both accounts use the same model name.","Attribute dispersion to cash-flow timing, constraints and implementation before concluding that security selection differed."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un même modèle produit des résultats différents avec flux, restrictions et exécution différents. La décomposition identifie la part contrôlable.","why":["La dispersion n’est pas une preuve de fraude.","Cela peut violer les contraintes du client.","Le nom ne suffit pas à expliquer les écarts.","Examine des causes concrètes et documentées."],"cue":"Même stratégie, exécutions et contraintes différentes.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/active-equity-investing-portfolio-construction","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b278","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-5.2","reading":"IM-5","concept":"Correlation and undiversified VaR","question":"Two zero-mean positions each have standalone normal VaR of EUR 6m at the same horizon and confidence. Their P&Ls are jointly normal with correlation −0.5. Portfolio VaR is closest to:","choices":["EUR 8.49m","EUR 0m","EUR 6m","EUR 12m"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Sous les mêmes paramètres normaux, VaR portefeuille=√(6²+6²+2×(−0,5)×6×6)=6m. La somme individuelle de 12m ignore la diversification.","why":["Correspond à une corrélation nulle.","Nécessiterait ici une corrélation de −1.","Intègre la covariance négative.","Donne la somme non diversifiée."],"cue":"Additionner les variances et la covariance.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"Math.sqrt(6*6+6*6+2*(-0.5)*6*6)","value":6,"optionValue":6,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b279","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-5.3","reading":"IM-5","concept":"Negative marginal VaR","question":"A small new hedge has marginal VaR of −0.12 euros per euro of position at current holdings. Under the local linear approximation, increasing the hedge notional by EUR 5m changes portfolio VaR by:","choices":["EUR +5m","EUR −0.60m","EUR +0.60m","EUR −5.12m"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Variation locale≈VaR marginale×variation de position=−0,12×5m=−0,60m. Ce résultat local ne garantit pas une réduction illimitée.","why":["Assimile notionnel et perte en risque.","Respecte le signe et l’échelle de la dérivée.","Perd l’effet de couverture.","Additionne des grandeurs incompatibles."],"cue":"Une contribution marginale négative couvre localement.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"-0.12*5","value":-0.6,"optionValue":-0.6,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b280","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-5.4","reading":"IM-5","concept":"Variance-minimizing hedge size","question":"Portfolio P has variance 100 in squared currency units. A hedge instrument H has variance 25 and covariance with P of −20. For P+xH, what unconstrained x minimizes variance?","choices":["0.8","−0.8","4.0","0.2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Var(P+xH)=100+2x(−20)+25x². Dérivée=−40+50x=0, donc x=0,8.","why":["Utilise −Cov(P,H)/Var(H).","Inverse le signe de la couverture.","Divise les variances sans covariance.","Prend l’inverse d’un ratio non pertinent."],"cue":"Position minimale = −covariance / variance du hedge.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"-(-20)/25","value":0.8,"optionValue":0.8,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b281","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-5.5","reading":"IM-5","concept":"Return per marginal risk","question":"Two feasible small investments each require the same capital. X adds expected return of 0.4m and marginal portfolio risk of 0.2m; Y adds 0.3m and 0.1m. All other constraints are slack and these risk changes are positive. Which is preferred for incremental return per unit of risk?","choices":["X, solely because its expected return is larger.","They are equivalent because capital requirements match.","Neither can be compared without their standalone VaRs.","Y, because its return-to-incremental-risk ratio is 3 rather than 2."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le critère marginal donne X=0,4/0,2=2 et Y=0,3/0,1=3. La covariance déjà incluse dans le risque marginal importe plus que le risque autonome.","why":["Ignore le risque ajouté.","Même capital ne signifie pas même efficacité.","Les risques marginaux fournis suffisent au critère posé.","Compare le gain au coût en risque portefeuille."],"cue":"Allouer sur le rendement par risque ajouté.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b282","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-6.1","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Risk budget versus capital budget","question":"An investment committee assigns 50% of capital to each of two managers and calls this an equal risk budget. Manager A has three times B’s volatility. Correlation is not specified. What is the best response?","choices":["Only each manager’s expected return is needed.","Risk budgets cannot be defined for active managers.","Equal capital is not equal risk; unequal volatilities give unequal contributions here, and covariance affects their magnitudes.","Equal capital guarantees equal risk under every covariance matrix."],"answer":2,"explanation":"À poids égaux, la différence des contributions à la variance est proportionnelle à σA²−σB² : la covariance commune se compense dans cette différence. Les contributions sont donc inégales ici; la covariance affecte néanmoins leurs niveaux.","why":["Les rendements ne déterminent pas le risque de covariance.","On peut allouer du tracking error aux gérants.","Les volatilités inégales suffisent à exclure l’égalité ici; les covariances affectent les contributions mesurées.","Faux dès que les risques et covariances diffèrent."],"cue":"Poids en capital ≠ poids en risque.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b283","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-6.2","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Horizon turnover and leverage","question":"A manager funds a leveraged five-year convergence trade with overnight borrowing and reports only one-day unlevered VaR. Which gap is most material?","choices":["Turnover is irrelevant when the trade is intended to converge.","The measure omits financing rollover and the effect of leverage over the time needed to realize or liquidate the trade.","A long expected holding period guarantees overnight funding renewal.","Unlevered one-day VaR automatically captures all margin calls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le calendrier du financement et celui de réalisation du gain diffèrent. Le levier et les appels de marge peuvent forcer une sortie avant convergence.","why":["Une liquidation contrainte crée du turnover inattendu.","Relie horizon d’investissement et horizon de survie.","Le prêteur peut ne pas renouveler.","Une VaR non leveragée n’intègre pas toute la trésorerie."],"cue":"La convergence n’assure pas la survie du financement.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b284","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-6.3","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Pension liability investment process","question":"A defined-benefit pension board chooses its strategic allocation using only asset return forecasts. Benefits are contractually due over decades. Which input must be incorporated first to frame the allocation?","choices":["Liability cash flows, funding objectives and sponsor ability to absorb shortfalls.","Only the average return of the best-performing asset class last year.","A rule that asset volatility must always be zero.","The assumption that pension contributions cannot change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le placement doit servir les prestations et la contrainte de financement. La capacité du sponsor et le calendrier des passifs encadrent le risque acceptable.","why":["Replace les actifs dans leur objectif économique.","Un classement passé ignore les engagements.","Un risque nul n’est ni requis ni toujours réalisable.","Les contributions et leur flexibilité doivent être étudiées."],"cue":"Partir du passif et de la capacité du sponsor.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b285","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-6.4","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Hedge fund transparency and budgets","question":"A pension allocates a low risk budget to a hedge fund using monthly smoothed NAV returns, despite opaque leverage and quarterly redemption gates. What additional analysis is most important?","choices":["Assume gates lower the economic volatility of underlying assets.","Treat monthly NAV autocorrelation as proof of stable alpha.","Replace due diligence with the fund’s target return.","Obtain position or factor exposures, financing terms and liquidity stress evidence rather than relying on reported volatility alone."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le lissage peut minimiser la volatilité publiée. Les expositions réelles, le levier et les conditions de sortie déterminent la vulnérabilité économique.","why":["Une restriction de rachat ne stabilise pas l’actif.","L’autocorrélation peut refléter des prix retardés.","Un objectif commercial n’est pas une mesure de risque.","Complète une mesure statistique peu informative."],"cue":"Le risque économique dépasse la série de NAV.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b286","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-6.5","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Sponsor risk in pension assets","question":"An airline sponsors a pension plan heavily invested in airlines and travel firms. Which risk is amplified beyond ordinary asset volatility?","choices":["A guaranteed reduction in funding risk through industry expertise.","No additional risk because sponsor and pension are separate entities.","Sponsor risk: contributions may be least available when plan assets and the sponsor’s business deteriorate together.","Only currency risk, even when every position is domestic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un choc sectoriel peut simultanément réduire les actifs du régime et la capacité de cotisation. Cette dépendance aggrave le financement.","why":["L’expertise ne supprime pas une exposition commune.","La séparation juridique n’efface pas la dépendance économique.","Relie santé du sponsor et besoins du régime.","Le mécanisme existe sans change."],"cue":"Le sponsor doit pouvoir aider quand les actifs baissent.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b287","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-6.6","reading":"IM-6","concept":"VaR monitoring limits","question":"A fund remains below its 99% one-day VaR limit, but has a large position that would take three weeks to sell in stress. Which monitoring response is strongest?","choices":["Interpret 99% VaR as the maximum possible loss.","Keep the VaR limit and add liquidity-horizon, concentration and tail-loss stress measures.","Conclude no additional risk exists below the VaR limit.","Replace the position’s liquidation horizon with one day by definition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La VaR à un jour ne décrit ni les queues au-delà du quantile ni le coût d’une liquidation longue. Des limites complémentaires sont nécessaires.","why":["Un quantile n’est pas une borne de perte.","Conserve une mesure utile en couvrant ses angles morts.","Une limite respectée ne couvre pas tous les risques.","Le marché détermine la durée de liquidation."],"cue":"Un quantile court ne décrit pas une sortie longue.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b288","topic":"investment","skill":"i-allocate","objective":"IM-6.7","reading":"IM-6","concept":"Risk guidelines look-through","question":"A pension permits derivatives only for hedging. A manager meets the cash equity weight limit but uses futures to double effective equity exposure. Which guideline most directly closes the gap?","choices":["Measure aggregate economic exposure and risk including derivatives, with purpose and leverage controls.","Apply position limits only to cash instruments.","Exclude futures because their initial cash payment is small.","Use the number of derivative contracts without notional or sensitivity adjustments."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Des limites fondées sur les expositions économiques empêchent de contourner le mandat par le faible décaissement initial d’un dérivé.","why":["Couvre les positions par transparence économique.","Laisse précisément la faille décrite.","La marge initiale n’est pas l’exposition au sous-jacent.","Les contrats diffèrent par taille et sensibilité."],"cue":"Contrôler l’exposition, pas seulement le cash investi.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b289","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-7.5","reading":"IM-7","concept":"Returns-based versus holdings-based style","question":"A fund uses derivatives to vary market exposure daily. Its quarterly holdings list shows few equities, but daily returns are strongly equity-sensitive. Which conclusion best reconciles the evidence?","choices":["The return regression must be false because the holdings list is authoritative for every day.","Low cash equity holdings prove low economic equity exposure.","Style analysis can identify the exact derivative trades uniquely from returns.","Returns-based style can detect effective exposures absent from a snapshot of cash holdings; derivative look-through is needed."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Un inventaire trimestriel peut manquer les dérivés et la variation intrapériode. Les rendements renseignent les sensibilités sans identifier chaque instrument.","why":["Un instantané n’est pas un historique complet.","Les dérivés changent l’exposition avec peu de cash.","Plusieurs portefeuilles peuvent produire des rendements similaires.","Combine deux sources d’information complémentaires."],"cue":"Comparer les expositions économiques aux instantanés.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/portfolio-performance-evaluation","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b290","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-7.6","reading":"IM-7","concept":"Survivorship in manager appraisal","question":"A database removes liquidated funds and backfills only the successful track records of new entrants. An analyst compares its average alpha with zero. Which concern is strongest?","choices":["Backfilled returns are always conservative.","A large number of surviving funds removes sample selection bias.","Survivorship and backfill selection can bias measured performance upward before any skill test.","Liquidated funds must have the same returns as surviving funds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Exclure les échecs et ajouter des historiques sélectionnés modifie la population observée. La taille de l’échantillon ne corrige pas cette sélection.","why":["Les historiques retenus peuvent favoriser les succès.","Le biais persiste même avec beaucoup d’observations.","Identifie les deux mécanismes de biais.","Leurs performances peuvent être systématiquement différentes."],"cue":"Un grand échantillon sélectionné reste biaisé.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/portfolio-performance-evaluation","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b291","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-7.7","reading":"IM-7","concept":"Window dressing of Sharpe","question":"A manager improves the reported Sharpe ratio by selling deep out-of-the-money puts during a sample with no major market fall. Which appraisal is most appropriate?","choices":["Any strategy with positive average return must have positive economic alpha.","The higher Sharpe may reward hidden negative skewness and unobserved tail losses rather than superior skill.","The ratio proves that tail risk fell.","Option premiums are risk-free returns until the first loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une petite prime fréquente peut masquer une perte rare très grande. Le ratio moyenne/écart-type n’évalue pas à lui seul cette asymétrie.","why":["Un rendement positif peut être simple compensation du risque.","Cherche la distribution et le risque hors échantillon.","Le risque de queue peut avoir augmenté.","Une prime rémunère une obligation contingente."],"cue":"Un Sharpe élevé peut vendre une catastrophe.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/portfolio-performance-evaluation","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b292","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-7.8","reading":"IM-7","concept":"Quadratic market timing payoff","question":"A Treynor–Mazuy model specifies portfolio excess return as alpha + beta×market excess return + gamma×(market excess return)^2. Returns are decimals. If gamma=2 and market excess return is −10%, the fitted timing contribution alone is:","choices":["+2%","−20%","−2%","+20%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Contribution de timing=2×(−0,10)²=0,02=2 %. Le carré rend ce terme positif dans les deux directions si gamma est positif.","why":["Convertit correctement le terme quadratique en pourcentage.","Utilise beta linéaire au lieu de gamma.","Conserve à tort le signe négatif après le carré.","Mauvaise échelle entre décimal et pourcentage."],"cue":"Timing quadratique : gamma × marché au carré.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/portfolio-performance-evaluation","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"2*((-0.10)**2)*100","value":2,"optionValue":2,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b293","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-7.9","reading":"IM-7","concept":"Brinson allocation effect","question":"A sector’s portfolio weight is 30% and benchmark weight 20%. The sector benchmark return is 8%; total benchmark return is 5%. Under the Brinson–Fachler allocation formula (wp−wb)×(rb,sector−rb,total), the sector allocation effect is:","choices":["+0.80 percentage points","+3.00 percentage points","−0.30 percentage points","+0.30 percentage points"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Effet allocation=(0,30−0,20)×(8−5)=0,30 point. La surpondération d’un secteur supérieur au benchmark apporte un effet positif.","why":["Omet le rendement du benchmark total.","Oublie de pondérer le différentiel sectoriel.","Inverse le signe de la surpondération.","Applique la formule avec les poids décimaux."],"cue":"Allocation : surpoids × rendement relatif du secteur.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/portfolio-performance-evaluation","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"(0.30-0.20)*(8-5)","value":0.3,"optionValue":0.3,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b294","topic":"investment","skill":"i-alpha","objective":"IM-8.1","reading":"IM-8","concept":"Discretionary macro strategy","question":"A fund expresses a view that country A will tighten monetary policy more than country B by trading their interest-rate futures and currencies. Which strategy description fits best?","choices":["Merger arbitrage with a known acquisition consideration.","Convertible arbitrage with delta hedging of a bond option.","Global macro: directional or relative exposures driven by macroeconomic views.","Equity market neutral based solely on firm earnings revisions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les positions sont choisies à partir de vues sur les politiques monétaires et leurs effets sur taux et changes. Elles relèvent d’une stratégie macro.","why":["Aucune opération de fusion n’est présente.","Aucun convertible n’est mentionné.","Correspond aux facteurs et instruments du cas.","Aucune sélection relative d’actions n’est décrite."],"cue":"Identifier le moteur économique du pari.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b295","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-8.2","reading":"IM-8","concept":"Convertible hedge adjustment","question":"A convertible position has equity delta equivalent to 40,000 shares, hedged with 40,000 shares sold short. After a stock rally, convertible delta rises to 55,000 shares. To restore local delta neutrality, ignoring other positions, the manager should:","choices":["Leave the hedge unchanged because it was initially neutral.","Sell short 15,000 additional shares.","Buy 15,000 shares.","Sell short 55,000 additional shares."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Delta net après hausse=55 000−40 000=+15 000 actions. Vendre 15 000 actions supplémentaires rétablit la neutralité locale.","why":["La convexité fait varier delta.","Compense l’exposition delta ajoutée.","Augmente encore le delta net.","Confond hedge total et ajustement supplémentaire."],"cue":"Delta neutral aujourd’hui doit être réajusté demain.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"55000-40000","value":15000,"optionValue":15000,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b296","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-8.3","reading":"IM-8","concept":"Stock-for-stock merger hedge","question":"An acquirer offers 0.5 of its shares for each target share. A merger arbitrageur buys 20,000 target shares and wants to hedge the promised stock consideration, conditional on completion. Ignoring basis and deal failure risk, the hedge is:","choices":["Short 10,000 acquirer shares.","Long 10,000 acquirer shares.","Short 40,000 acquirer shares.","Short 20,000 target shares."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La contrepartie attendue est 20 000×0,5=10 000 actions acquéreur. Une vente à découvert de ce montant couvre le risque de leur prix conditionnellement à la réussite.","why":["Réplique le nombre d’actions à recevoir avec signe opposé.","Ajoute l’exposition plutôt que la couvrir.","Inverse le ratio d’échange.","Annule la position cible au lieu de couvrir la contrepartie."],"cue":"Hedge stock deal = cible × ratio d’échange.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"20000*0.5","value":10000,"optionValue":10000,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b297","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-8.4","reading":"IM-8","concept":"Distressed debt control rights","question":"A distressed fund buys the debt class expected to receive most equity in a restructuring. Which due diligence item is most critical to the proposed debt-to-control strategy?","choices":["Only the debt’s original coupon rate.","The assumption that the cheapest debt always receives control.","The issuer’s pre-distress stock index membership.","Priority, collateral value, creditor voting rights and the reorganization valuation under the applicable process."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La dette pivot dépend de la valeur réorganisée et de la cascade de priorité. Les droits de vote et garanties influencent aussi la négociation.","why":["Le coupon ne suffit pas à déterminer le pouvoir.","Une dette très décotée peut ne rien récupérer.","L’indice ne définit ni priorité ni droit de vote.","Relie récupération et contrôle aux droits réels."],"cue":"Le contrôle dépend de la classe pivot et des droits.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b298","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-9.1","reading":"IM-9","concept":"Hedge fund investor liquidity risk","question":"A hedge fund invests in assets liquidatable over six months but offers monthly redemptions subject to a discretionary gate. An investor counts on full redemption next month. What is the strongest correction?","choices":["A monthly dealing frequency guarantees daily market liquidity in assets.","The gate protects the investor from any economic loss.","The gate and asset-liability liquidity mismatch make the expected cash date uncertain even if the latest NAV is positive.","A positive NAV makes the redemption date certain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une date de rachat contractuelle peut être restreinte. La liquidité de l’actif et les modalités du fonds déterminent l’accès effectif au cash.","why":["La fréquence de dealing ne transforme pas l’actif.","La gate retarde la sortie sans garantir la valeur.","Distingue valeur et disponibilité du placement.","Solvabilité apparente et liquidité sont distinctes."],"cue":"NAV positive ne signifie pas cash disponible.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b299","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-9.2","reading":"IM-9","concept":"Crowded hedge fund deleveraging","question":"Several funds hold the same leveraged relative-value trade through different prime brokers. A price shock triggers simultaneous margin calls. Which channel can amplify systemic losses?","choices":["Losses remain confined to initial equity investors by definition.","Common forced sales depress collateral prices, triggering further margin calls and losses at connected counterparties.","Different prime brokers ensure that collateral prices cannot be correlated.","A market-neutral label prevents financing stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Des liquidations communes font baisser les prix utilisés comme garanties. Cela peut créer une spirale marge-prix et transmettre les pertes aux financeurs.","why":["Les contreparties et prix de marché sont connectés.","Décrit la rétroaction commune aux bilans.","La séparation des courtiers ne sépare pas le marché.","Neutralité directionnelle et financement sont différents."],"cue":"Même trade + levier = boucle de liquidation possible.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b300","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-9.3","reading":"IM-9","concept":"Regulatory leverage transparency","question":"A supervisor seeks to identify common leveraged exposures across hedge funds and prime brokers. Which measure most directly supports that objective?","choices":["Consistent reporting of derivatives, financing, counterparties and economic leverage, combined with aggregation across firms.","Collect only fund names and registered addresses.","Prohibit disclosure of counterparty identities to the supervisor.","Require only each fund’s unadjusted NAV return volatility."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le risque commun apparaît en rapprochant les positions et relations de financement. Des données comparables sont nécessaires à l’agrégation.","why":["Mesure les liens et expositions ciblés.","Ces informations ne décrivent aucun risque de bilan.","Empêche de reconstruire le réseau.","Une série lissée ne révèle pas le levier global."],"cue":"Une surveillance du réseau exige des données comparables.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b301","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-9.4","reading":"IM-9","concept":"Master-feeder economic structure","question":"Two feeder funds catering to different investor tax categories invest into one master fund that holds the trading positions. What is the main economic benefit of this structure?","choices":["It eliminates underlying investment risk through legal multiplication.","It ensures each feeder holds an independently diversified trading portfolio.","It makes all investor tax treatment identical across jurisdictions.","It pools trading and portfolio management while allowing different investor-facing vehicles."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le master centralise les opérations; les feeders adaptent l’accès aux catégories d’investisseurs. Les risques des positions sous-jacentes restent communs.","why":["Changer l’enveloppe n’annule pas le risque.","Les positions sont précisément réunies dans le master.","Les différences fiscales motivent souvent les feeders.","Distingue mutualisation opérationnelle et structure investisseur."],"cue":"Plusieurs accès investisseurs, un portefeuille master.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b302","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-10.1","reading":"IM-10","concept":"Private credit versus syndicated loans","question":"A midsize sponsor-owned firm needs a bespoke floating-rate loan held by a small group of nonbank lenders. Which feature most distinguishes typical direct private credit from a broadly syndicated liquid loan?","choices":["A guarantee that the borrower is investment grade.","A requirement that lenders fund exclusively with insured deposits.","Direct negotiation, limited secondary trading and lender-specific monitoring arrangements.","Mandatory daily exchange trading and standardized retail order books."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le crédit privé est généralement négocié bilatéralement ou en petit groupe et peu échangé. Il répond notamment à des besoins de financement adaptés.","why":["Les emprunteurs peuvent être risqués et endettés.","Les fonds ne sont pas des banques de dépôts.","Décrit les caractéristiques de la relation privée.","Décrit plutôt un marché standardisé liquide."],"cue":"Prêt négocié et relation de suivi, faible liquidité.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/gfsr/issues/2024/04/16/global-financial-stability-report-april-2024","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b303","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-10.2","reading":"IM-10","concept":"Private credit return comparison","question":"A private credit index has higher reported returns and lower reported quarterly volatility than a public high-yield index. Which comparison is most defensible?","choices":["Assume private and public borrowers have identical characteristics.","Adjust for fees, leverage, borrower risk, illiquidity and valuation smoothing before inferring superior risk-adjusted performance.","Infer strict dominance directly from the two reported moments.","Treat the absence of daily marks as proof of lower economic risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les conventions de prix et expositions diffèrent. Une comparaison brute peut attribuer à la gestion des primes de risque ou un lissage.","why":["La sélection des emprunteurs peut différer.","Cherche une comparaison économique cohérente.","Les deux statistiques ne suffisent pas.","Une fréquence de prix faible masque parfois le risque."],"cue":"Comparer des risques et des prix comparables.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/gfsr/issues/2024/04/16/global-financial-stability-report-april-2024","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b304","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-10.3","reading":"IM-10","concept":"Private credit bank interconnection","question":"A bank has no direct loans to private-credit borrowers but provides revolving facilities to their funds and loans to fund investors. Why can a corporate downturn still affect the bank?","choices":["Fund drawdowns, collateral deterioration and investor stress can transmit the underlying credit shock through indirect links.","Only direct borrower loans can generate credit exposure.","Fund commitments cannot be drawn during a downturn.","Illiquid loan marks always adjust before bank funding needs arise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les lignes aux fonds et aux investisseurs créent des canaux de transmission distincts du prêt à l’entreprise finale. Les besoins de financement peuvent augmenter en crise.","why":["Suit les engagements et contreparties intermédiaires.","Ignore le financement du réseau.","Les tirages peuvent précisément augmenter en stress.","Les valorisations peuvent réagir avec retard."],"cue":"L’absence de prêt direct n’efface pas le lien financier.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/gfsr/issues/2024/04/16/global-financial-stability-report-april-2024","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b305","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-10.4","reading":"IM-10","concept":"Private credit policy data gap","question":"Authorities cannot reconcile fund leverage, bank financing and exposures to common private borrowers. Which first policy priority best addresses the stated vulnerability?","choices":["Infer aggregate safety from a low public default count alone.","Assume closed-end structures eliminate every financial-stability channel.","Require daily investor redemptions regardless of asset liquidity.","Improve consistent reporting and supervisory information sharing across funds, banks and jurisdictions."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Des informations rapprochables permettent de mesurer concentration, levier et interconnexions. Une structure fermée aide la liquidité sans éliminer ces risques.","why":["Un défaut publié ne mesure pas tout le réseau.","Elle ne supprime ni pertes de crédit ni levier.","Cela peut aggraver la transformation de liquidité.","Cible la lacune de données décrite."],"cue":"Mesurer les liens avant de juger le risque global.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/gfsr/issues/2024/04/16/global-financial-stability-report-april-2024","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b306","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-11.1","reading":"IM-11","concept":"Private market investment motivation","question":"A sovereign wealth fund with stable long-term funding considers private infrastructure. Which rationale is most defensible?","choices":["A promise that every private investment outperforms public markets.","The ability to liquidate all holdings immediately at reported NAV.","Potential access to distinct cash flows and governance opportunities, provided expected compensation exceeds fees and illiquidity costs.","A guarantee that infrequent prices eliminate economic volatility."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un horizon long peut aider à supporter l’illiquidité. Il faut néanmoins comparer les avantages aux frais, risques et contraintes réels.","why":["Aucune surperformance universelle n’existe.","La NAV n’est pas un engagement de rachat instantané.","Formule un avantage potentiel conditionnel.","Le risque demeure même sans cotation."],"cue":"Un horizon long permet l’illiquidité, sans la rendre gratuite.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/private-investments-structures","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b307","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-11.2","reading":"IM-11","concept":"Closed-end commitment structure","question":"An investor commits EUR 20m to a ten-year closed-end private equity fund; only EUR 6m is called initially. Which statement is correct?","choices":["An uncalled commitment is identical to a liquid cash asset owned by the fund.","The remaining commitment can create future cash obligations even though it is not yet invested NAV.","Only EUR 6m can ever be required because that is the initial NAV.","The investor can redeem the full commitment daily at par."],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’engagement non appelé demeure une obligation conditionnelle. Il doit être intégré à la planification de trésorerie, séparément de la valeur investie.","why":["Le cash demeure chez l’investisseur jusqu’à l’appel.","Distingue engagement et capital effectivement appelé.","Ignore les appels futurs prévus au contrat.","Un fonds fermé n’offre pas ce rachat quotidien."],"cue":"Engagement non appelé = besoin de cash possible.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/private-investments-structures","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b308","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-11.4","reading":"IM-11","concept":"Commitment liquidity stress","question":"A private-market investor has EUR 15m liquid assets, EUR 9m expected capital calls and EUR 4m stressed cash needs elsewhere. Expected fund distributions of EUR 6m are assumed to stop in stress. Ignoring all other flows, stressed residual liquidity is:","choices":["EUR 2m","EUR 8m","EUR 6m","EUR 24m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Liquidité stressée=15−9−4=2m. Les distributions supposées nulles ne doivent pas financer les besoins dans ce scénario.","why":["Exclut les distributions interrompues et déduit tous les besoins.","Ajoute les distributions ordinaires malgré le stress.","Omet les autres besoins de cash.","Ajoute les appels au lieu de les déduire."],"cue":"Tester appels sans distributions quand les marchés chutent.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/private-investments-structures","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"15-9-4","value":2,"optionValue":2,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b309","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-11.5","reading":"IM-11","concept":"Co-investment adverse selection","question":"A limited partner is offered a large fee-reduced co-investment alongside its general partner. Its team has little time to assess the single company. Which assessment is best?","choices":["Lower fees eliminate the need for company due diligence.","Co-investment automatically diversifies a concentrated portfolio.","The general partner’s participation guarantees the exit price.","Lower fees can help, but concentration, execution capacity and deal-selection incentives still require independent review."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le co-investissement réduit parfois les frais mais concentre l’exposition dans un seul actif. L’alignement et la capacité d’analyse restent à vérifier.","why":["Les risques opérationnels et économiques demeurent.","Une ligne unique peut accroître la concentration.","La participation n’est pas une garantie de sortie.","Pèse économies et risques propres au deal."],"cue":"Moins de frais ne remplace pas l’analyse du deal.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/private-investments-structures","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b310","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-11.6","reading":"IM-11","concept":"Intermediated private fund fees","question":"A new institution can invest directly in five private companies or through a diversified private equity fund. Which tradeoff most directly favors the fund despite its additional fee layer?","choices":["Immediate redemption at an exchange price.","Elimination of agency conflicts between manager and investor.","Access to specialized sourcing, monitoring and a broader investment program, balanced against fees and reduced control.","A legal guarantee of positive returns in every vintage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une équipe spécialisée peut fournir accès et suivi difficiles à reproduire. En contrepartie, l’investisseur supporte des frais et délègue des décisions.","why":["La structure privée reste généralement illiquide.","La délégation crée aussi des conflits à gérer.","Compare bénéfice d’intermédiation et son coût.","Aucun fonds n’assure chaque millésime."],"cue":"Accès et expertise contre frais et contrôle.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/private-investments-structures","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b311","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-12.1","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Convergence fund failure mechanism","question":"A leveraged relative-value fund correctly expects two bond prices to converge in a year. Before convergence, its losses widen, counterparties increase margins and financing is withdrawn. What most directly explains failure despite the long-run view being right?","choices":["Diversification across many trades guarantees access to financing.","Funding and market-liquidity risk can force liquidation before an economically plausible convergence occurs.","Its forecast must have been wrong because every correctly priced trade can be held indefinitely.","Daily mark-to-market losses matter only after the forecast horizon."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un trade peut avoir une valeur terminale positive mais manquer de cash avant cette date. Les marges et retraits de financement imposent une liquidation défavorable.","why":["Des positions diversifiées peuvent partager un même financement fragile.","Relie survie du fonds et horizon de réalisation.","Une bonne prévision ne garantit pas le financement.","Les marges rendent les pertes intermédiaires immédiatement contraignantes."],"cue":"Être juste trop tôt peut coûter le financement.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b312","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-12.2","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Track record verification","question":"A prospective manager presents an excellent five-year record from a former employer. Which due diligence step best establishes whether that record is relevant to the proposed fund?","choices":["Verify the record independently and identify the team, mandate, capital and implementation conditions responsible for it.","Accept the slides if the reported Sharpe ratio exceeds two.","Compare only gross returns with a cash benchmark.","Assume the lead manager personally made every decision because they held the senior title."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Il faut confirmer les chiffres et leur attribuabilité. Une performance d’équipe avec un autre mandat ne se transfère pas automatiquement au nouveau véhicule.","why":["Vérifie existence et pertinence économique de l’historique.","Une statistique élevée n’est pas une preuve externe.","Les risques et coûts du mandat comptent.","Le titre hiérarchique ne prouve pas l’origine des décisions."],"cue":"Vérifier les chiffres et qui les a produits.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b313","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-12.3","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Manager capacity stress","question":"A small-cap strategy achieved strong returns at EUR 100m and is now raising EUR 2bn without changing its trading universe. Which question is most diagnostic of its ability to repeat performance?","choices":["Did the firm update its logo before fundraising?","Can the firm multiply every historical return by twenty?","Was the original return positive in its best month?","How do position sizes, market impact, turnover and opportunity capacity change as assets grow twentyfold?"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le même signal peut devenir inexploitable à grande taille. Il faut évaluer participation au volume, coûts et capacité de déploiement.","why":["Le branding ne mesure pas la capacité.","Un rendement n’est pas proportionnel au capital.","Un mois favorable ne teste pas le changement d’échelle.","Teste la contrainte économique nouvelle."],"cue":"Une stratégie a une capacité, pas seulement un Sharpe.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b314","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-12.4","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Risk limit governance","question":"A hedge fund’s head trader can override all risk limits without documentation and also approves the stress scenarios. Which change most directly improves the risk-management process?","choices":["Replacing written limits with a verbal statement of caution.","Using only the trader’s most favorable historical scenario.","Independent risk oversight, recorded escalation and enforceable limits with stress tests challenging trading assumptions.","A higher VaR limit approved by the same trader."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un contrôle indépendant et une procédure de dérogation traçable limitent l’auto-validation. Les stress doivent contester les hypothèses du trading.","why":["Diminue la traçabilité.","Sélectionne le scénario pour éviter le risque.","Renforce gouvernance et capacité de contradiction.","Accroît la discrétion sans contrôle."],"cue":"Un contrôle doit pouvoir contredire le preneur de risque.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b315","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-12.5","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Operational reconciliation breaks","question":"A fund’s front office marks OTC trades, keeps the cash ledger and reconciles its own valuations with counterparties. Its auditor visits annually. Which operational improvement is most direct?","choices":["Reconcile only after investors submit redemption notices.","Separate valuation and reconciliation responsibilities, with timely independent verification of cash and positions.","Keep the structure because an annual audit substitutes for daily controls.","Give the front office exclusive authority over the auditor appointment and findings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le cumul des fonctions crée un risque d’erreur ou de dissimulation. La séparation et les rapprochements réguliers réduisent ce risque entre deux audits.","why":["Laisse les écarts s’accumuler sans détection.","Traite le conflit de fonctions décrit.","Un audit périodique ne remplace pas les contrôles courants.","Renforce la dépendance du contrôle au contrôlé."],"cue":"Indépendance et rapprochements réguliers.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b316","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-12.6","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Management company runway","question":"A fund manager’s management-company fixed costs are EUR 4m annually. Fee-paying assets are EUR 150m and its management fee is 1.5% annually. Ignore performance fees and all other income. The annual operating deficit is:","choices":["EUR 1.75m","EUR 2.25m","EUR 4.00m","EUR 0.25m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Revenus récurrents=150×1,5 %=2,25m. Déficit=4−2,25=1,75m. Le financement de la société de gestion doit être évalué séparément du fonds.","why":["Calcule coûts moins revenus stables.","Donne les revenus plutôt que le déficit.","Ignore les frais de gestion encaissés.","Erreur de conversion ou de soustraction."],"cue":"La société de gestion doit aussi survivre.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"4-150*0.015","value":1.75,"optionValue":1.75,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b317","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-12.7","reading":"IM-12","concept":"Due diligence questionnaire evidence","question":"A DDQ asks who prices hard-to-value assets and how disputed prices are escalated. The manager replies only, “all returns are audited.” What is the best follow-up?","choices":["Delete the question because an audit answers every operational detail.","Request only a longer marketing presentation.","Infer that no hard-to-value positions exist because none are listed in the reply.","Request valuation policies, independent pricing sources, override logs and responsibilities for resolving disputes."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La réponse ne décrit pas le processus demandé. Les pièces et responsabilités permettent de vérifier les pratiques au-delà d’une déclaration générale.","why":["L’audit ne décrit pas toute la chaîne quotidienne.","Ne fournit pas d’élément probant.","L’absence de réponse ne prouve pas l’absence d’actifs.","Transforme la question en vérifications concrètes."],"cue":"Un DDQ demande des preuves, pas un slogan.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/investment-manager-selection","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b318","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-13.1","reading":"IM-13","concept":"Distress despite positive EBITDA","question":"A firm has positive EBITDA of EUR 12m but cash interest of EUR 10m, mandatory principal repayments of EUR 8m and no available refinancing. Ignore taxes, capex and working-capital changes. Which assessment is best?","choices":["It has EUR 2m surplus after all debt service.","Principal repayments reduce accounting EBITDA before the calculation.","It has a EUR 6m cash debt-service shortfall despite positive EBITDA.","Positive EBITDA excludes financial distress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Ressource simplifiée=12m, service de dette=10+8=18m, déficit=6m. La rentabilité d’exploitation ne garantit pas la liquidité.","why":["Omet les remboursements de principal.","Le principal est un flux financier, pas une charge EBITDA.","Intègre intérêt et principal.","Un résultat positif n’assure pas le paiement des échéances."],"cue":"Le cash doit couvrir intérêt ET principal.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"10+8-12","value":6,"optionValue":6,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b319","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-13.2","reading":"IM-13","concept":"Workout coordination versus liquidation","question":"A viable business is worth 120 as a going concern but only 80 in liquidation. Debt due now is 100 and creditors are fragmented. What is the strongest rationale for a coordinated restructuring?","choices":["Liquidation must always be preferred whenever debt is due.","It may preserve going-concern value by modifying claims, but creditor coordination and credible viability remain necessary.","It creates value simply by changing every debt claim into cash immediately.","The higher going-concern estimate guarantees unanimous creditor agreement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un accord sur les échéances ou créances peut éviter de détruire 40 de valeur économique. Les désaccords entre créanciers et l’incertitude de valorisation demeurent.","why":["L’exigibilité n’impose pas que la liquidation maximise la valeur.","Identifie le gain potentiel et les obstacles.","Une restructuration ne produit pas du cash sans financement.","Des intérêts et priorités différents créent des conflits."],"cue":"Préserver la valeur exige aussi de coordonner les droits.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b320","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-13.3","reading":"IM-13","concept":"Cross-border restructuring enforcement","question":"A distressed group’s assets and creditors span two jurisdictions with different recognition and security-enforcement rules. A proposed plan assumes a single domestic court decision binds every creditor everywhere. What is the key challenge?","choices":["Recognition, priority and enforcement may differ across jurisdictions and must be assessed before relying on the global recovery estimate.","The group’s consolidated accounts automatically impose one insolvency law worldwide.","All secured creditors have identical rights regardless of asset location.","An accounting impairment determines the legally enforceable payout."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les droits et effets d’une décision ne se propagent pas automatiquement à toutes les juridictions. La récupération dépend de leur reconnaissance et de l’exécution.","why":["Teste l’hypothèse juridique du plan.","Une consolidation comptable n’unifie pas les droits.","Les sûretés et règles locales peuvent différer.","Une valeur comptable n’est pas un jugement de distribution."],"cue":"La consolidation comptable n’unifie pas le droit.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b321","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-14.1","reading":"IM-14","concept":"Reported split-strike strategy verification","question":"A manager claims to replicate Madoff’s reported split-strike conversion approach. Which position pattern would an investigator expect to seek in independent records for that claimed strategy?","choices":["Only long Treasury bills with no equity or option transactions.","A pure trend-following futures portfolio with no options.","Only short equities with no long assets or hedges.","A basket of equities combined with protective puts and written calls."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le schéma annoncé associait actions, achats de puts et ventes de calls. Vérifier ces positions attendues sert à confronter le récit aux preuves, pas à valider un historique de rendement.","why":["Ne reproduit pas la stratégie revendiquée.","Décrit un autre type de gestion.","Ne correspond pas à la protection et au financement annoncés.","Correspond au montage optionnel annoncé."],"cue":"Comparer le récit de stratégie aux transactions indépendantes.","source":"https://www.sec.gov/files/oig-509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b322","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-14.2","reading":"IM-14","concept":"Independent custody red flag","question":"A manager reports unusually smooth returns, uses a small related auditor and refuses direct custodian confirmation, citing secrecy. Which response is most appropriate?","choices":["Use the smooth return series as a substitute for custody evidence.","Increase the allocation because an obscure auditor implies lower costs.","Treat the combination as a serious red flag and require independent asset and transaction verification before committing.","Accept secrecy as sufficient evidence of a proprietary edge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La combinaison de performances peu plausibles et de contrôles indépendants faibles justifie une vérification renforcée. Un red flag ne constitue pas seul une preuve définitive de fraude.","why":["Un chiffre publié ne prouve pas l’existence des actifs.","Les frais d’audit ne justifient pas l’absence de contrôle.","Demande la preuve qui manque sans conclure prématurément.","Un secret de trading n’interdit pas une confirmation d’actifs."],"cue":"Un bon rendement ne remplace pas une preuve de garde.","source":"https://www.sec.gov/files/oig-509.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b323","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-15.1","reading":"IM-15","concept":"Market-driven scenario conditioning","question":"A risk team starts with a specified severe equity shock and uses estimated joint market relationships to infer coherent moves in other factors. What is the main purpose of this market-driven scenario design?","choices":["Prove that any event outside the scenario is impossible.","Translate a chosen market disturbance into a joint scenario informed by cross-factor dependence.","Forecast the exact date of the next crisis.","Set every other factor to its individual worst historical move regardless of dependence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La méthode construit un scénario joint autour d’un événement moteur en utilisant les relations de marché. Elle n’est ni une date de prévision ni une frontière absolue des pertes.","why":["Un modèle de scénario n’épuise pas les événements possibles.","Décrit la logique conditionnelle de construction.","La conception d’un stress ne date pas les crises.","Cela peut produire une combinaison incohérente."],"cue":"Partir d’un choc moteur et reconstruire les liens.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b324","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-15.4","reading":"IM-15","concept":"Stress scenario model uncertainty","question":"A market-driven stress scenario uses covariance estimated entirely in a tranquil period and assumes linear relationships. It produces a small loss for a portfolio with short options. Which challenge should receive priority?","choices":["Dependence and nonlinear payoffs may change in stress, so challenge both the joint scenario and full repricing assumptions.","A small modeled loss means the portfolio cannot suffer a larger loss.","Historical covariance uniquely determines every tail event.","Short options can be repriced reliably using constant delta for any shock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les covariances calmes et la linéarité peuvent manquer corrélations de crise, volatilité et convexité. Il faut contester le scénario et réévaluer les instruments.","why":["Couvre les deux sources de sous-estimation du cas.","Un résultat conditionnel n’est pas une borne.","La covariance ne décrit pas toute la queue.","Delta varie fortement lors de grands mouvements."],"cue":"Stress : dépendances de crise et repricing non linéaire.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b325","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-16.1","reading":"IM-16","concept":"Fund liquidity governance","question":"An open-end bond fund’s portfolio team owns the liquidity model and may ignore its alerts to protect returns. Which governance arrangement best supports liquidity-risk management?","choices":["Liquidity review only after the first missed redemption.","A target return that overrides every liquidity limit.","One historical bid–ask spread as the sole measure.","Independent challenge, documented liquidity limits and escalation, aligned with redemption terms and investor interests."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La liquidité doit être suivie de façon prospective et intégrée aux conditions de rachat. Un contrôle indépendant et une escalade évitent l’arbitrage implicite contre la liquidité.","why":["Réagit après l’échec de paiement.","Écarte la fonction de contrôle.","Une mesure unique ne couvre pas profondeur et stress.","Relie gouvernance, limites et obligations du fonds."],"cue":"La liquidité est une contrainte de gouvernance.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b326","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-16.2","reading":"IM-16","concept":"Sparse bond liquidity observations","question":"A corporate bond did not trade for twelve days. A fund’s model treats its unchanged evaluated price as proof of zero market impact. What is the most appropriate correction?","choices":["Assign zero spread whenever a bond has no recent trade.","Use yesterday’s evaluated mark as a guaranteed executable bid for any size.","Use comparable instruments and stressed execution assumptions; a missing trade is not evidence of costless liquidity.","Infer infinite depth because the price was stable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Un prix évalué peut rester stable faute de transaction. Les proxys de liquidité doivent intégrer incertitude, taille et conditions de marché.","why":["L’absence de transaction ne renseigne pas un spread nul.","Une marque n’est pas une offre ferme pour toute taille.","Distingue absence d’observation et coût nul.","La stabilité peut précisément refléter l’illiquidité."],"cue":"Pas de transaction ne signifie pas coût nul.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b327","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-16.3","reading":"IM-16","concept":"Specified bond transaction-cost model","question":"A simplified bond t-cost model gives one-way cost in basis points as 8+3×sqrt(q/V), where q is order size and V daily volume in the same units. For q=4m and V=1m, the cost in basis points is:","choices":["6 bps","14 bps","20 bps","11 bps"],"answer":1,"explanation":"q/V=4, sa racine vaut 2. Coût=8+3×2=14 points de base. La formule fournie est un modèle simplifié propre au cas.","why":["Omet le coût de base de 8 bps.","Applique la racine avant le coefficient.","Utilise q/V sans racine.","Suppose q/V=1."],"cue":"Respecter unités, racine et coût de base.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":4,"numeric":{"expression":"8+3*Math.sqrt(4/1)","value":14,"optionValue":14,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b328","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-16.4","reading":"IM-16","concept":"Extraordinary redemption suspension","question":"Assume applicable rules permit temporary redemption suspension only under exceptional market conditions and with the required approvals. A bond fund cannot obtain reliable executable prices across a large part of its portfolio. Which action best respects that framework?","choices":["Assess whether the exceptional-condition criteria are met, seek the required approvals and communicate a documented temporary measure.","Suspend permanently without review because investment returns were disappointing.","Promise all investors full immediate payment at stale marks regardless of market conditions.","Use the measure solely to hide a manager’s relative underperformance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une mesure extraordinaire exige motif, procédure et communication. Elle doit répondre à la désorganisation de marché plutôt qu’à un simple objectif commercial.","why":["Suit les hypothèses réglementaires explicitement posées.","La condition exceptionnelle n’autorise pas un arrêt définitif arbitraire.","Cela peut transférer des pertes aux investisseurs restants.","La sous-performance ne suffit pas dans le cadre donné."],"cue":"Une mesure exceptionnelle exige justification et procédure.","source":"https://www.garp.org/landing/frm-learning-objectives","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b329","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-17.1","reading":"IM-17","concept":"Illiquid market price discovery","question":"Two appraisals value the same private asset similarly, but recent attempted sales clear only after long negotiation and large discounts. Which characteristic is most relevant?","choices":["Similar appraisals establish a continuously liquid two-way market.","An appraisal is always a firm bid from a buyer.","Long negotiation proves there is no information asymmetry.","Reported valuation consistency can coexist with high search costs, limited depth and uncertain executable prices."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La liquidité dépend de l’exécution, de la profondeur et du délai, pas seulement de la cohérence des valeurs estimées.","why":["Des estimations ne constituent pas un carnet d’ordres.","Une valeur évaluée n’engage aucun acheteur.","La négociation peut refléter l’asymétrie d’information.","Décrit les frictions observées."],"cue":"Évaluer un actif ne garantit pas pouvoir le vendre.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/asset-allocation-to-alternative-investments","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b330","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-17.2","reading":"IM-17","concept":"Adverse selection and illiquidity","question":"Potential buyers cannot distinguish good private loans from poor ones, while sellers know their quality. Buyers reduce bids, and high-quality sellers withdraw. Which mechanism best explains the resulting illiquidity?","choices":["Perfectly symmetric information guarantees the same outcome.","The number of calendar days since issue fully determines liquidity.","Adverse selection widens the valuation gap and discourages mutually beneficial trades.","Higher transparency causes good sellers to withdraw by definition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"L’asymétrie d’information fait baisser l’offre de prix. Le retrait des bons actifs dégrade encore la qualité perçue du marché.","why":["Ce mécanisme repose sur l’information privée.","L’âge ne remplace pas le mécanisme de qualité.","Décrit le mécanisme de sélection adverse.","Le cas suppose justement une information asymétrique."],"cue":"La crainte des mauvais actifs peut faire fuir les bons.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/asset-allocation-to-alternative-investments","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b331","topic":"investment","skill":"i-private","objective":"IM-17.5","reading":"IM-17","concept":"Estimating an illiquidity premium","question":"A private loan yields 10% and a public loan 7%. The private borrower is also more levered and its loan has weaker protections. Which conclusion is most defensible?","choices":["Subtracting the risk-free rate from both yields removes all credit-risk differences.","The 3-point spread cannot all be labeled an illiquidity premium without controlling credit risk and contractual differences.","The entire 3-point spread is necessarily pure liquidity compensation.","Illiquidity premiums must equal zero whenever credit risk exists."],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’écart de rendement mélange liquidité, risque de crédit et clauses. Une estimation de prime d’illiquidité exige des actifs comparables sur les autres dimensions.","why":["Le benchmark sans risque ne neutralise pas le risque spécifique du prêt.","Isole ce qui reste à identifier.","Attribue tout l’écart à une seule cause.","Les deux primes peuvent coexister."],"cue":"Comparer à risque de crédit et droits similaires.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/asset-allocation-to-alternative-investments","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b332","topic":"investment","skill":"i-stress","objective":"IM-17.6","reading":"IM-17","concept":"Denominator effect and rebalancing","question":"A portfolio starts with 60m public assets and 40m private assets. Public assets fall 25%; private marks initially remain 40m. Before any cash flows, the reported private weight is closest to:","choices":["47.1%","40.0%","53.3%","66.7%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Actifs publics=60×0,75=45m; total=85m; poids privé=40/85=47,06 %. Le rééquilibrage peut être difficile car les actifs privés restent peu liquides.","why":["Recalcule le dénominateur après la baisse.","Conserve le poids initial malgré le nouveau total.","Utilise une mauvaise base de comparaison.","Divise par les seuls actifs publics initiaux."],"cue":"Une baisse du liquide augmente le poids du privé.","source":"https://www.cfainstitute.org/insights/professional-learning/refresher-readings/2026/asset-allocation-to-alternative-investments","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"40/(60*(1-0.25)+40)*100","value":47.05882352941176,"optionValue":47.1,"tolerance":0.05}},{"id":"b333","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-1.1","reading":"CI-1","concept":"GenAI research workflow controls","question":"A broker uses a language model to summarize earnings calls for analysts. Before allowing summaries to trigger trades, which limitation is most directly relevant?","choices":["Summarization error is the same as ordinary bid–ask spread risk.","A model trained on public text necessarily has access to every unpublished earnings revision.","Text generation provides a calibrated probability of future stock returns without additional validation.","Fluent summaries can contain unsupported statements, so source verification and decision controls are needed."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La production de texte plausible ne garantit pas la fidélité aux sources. Le contrôle doit porter sur les faits utilisés avant une décision de marché.","why":["La liquidité n’explique pas une affirmation inventée.","Les informations non publiées ne sont pas disponibles par définition.","Une phrase n’est pas une probabilité financière calibrée.","Cible une erreur de contenu et son usage."],"cue":"Texte convaincant ≠ fait vérifié.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2024/10/22/global-financial-stability-report-october-2024","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b334","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-1.2","reading":"CI-1","concept":"AI liquidity in stress","question":"Several market makers adopt AI tools that quote tightly during normal conditions but withdraw when the same uncertainty threshold is crossed. What market-dynamics concern deserves stress testing?","choices":["Independent firm ownership implies independent trading responses.","Common thresholds reduce the need to simulate joint withdrawals.","Normal-time liquidity gains can coexist with abrupt common withdrawal and larger stressed price moves.","Tighter normal spreads establish equal depth during every future stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les améliorations en période normale ne prouvent pas une liquidité résiliente. Un signal partagé peut synchroniser le retrait de cotations.","why":["Des entités différentes peuvent suivre le même modèle.","Un seuil commun rend ce test plus pertinent.","Teste le changement de comportement en crise.","Le spread normal ne garantit pas la profondeur stressée."],"cue":"Tester quand les fournisseurs de liquidité s’arrêtent ensemble.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2024/10/22/global-financial-stability-report-october-2024","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b335","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-1.3","reading":"CI-1","concept":"Speed versus systemic control","question":"A dealer’s AI trading system reacts in milliseconds, while its exposure aggregation and kill-switch review update once per minute. What is the most direct financial-stability concern?","choices":["A successful single-trade validation rules out interaction effects.","Fast correlated actions can accumulate and transmit exposures before slower controls react.","Faster trading by itself ensures that aggregate exposures are always smaller.","A minute-level control necessarily observes every intraminute peak exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Une différence de vitesse peut laisser se développer une boucle de positions et de prix avant l’intervention des contrôles. Le test doit porter sur la dynamique jointe.","why":["Un trade isolé ne teste pas les interactions.","Compare les horizons d’action et de contrôle.","La vitesse ne fixe pas le signe du risque.","Des pics peuvent apparaître et disparaître entre deux mesures."],"cue":"Des contrôles plus lents que les actions laissent un angle mort.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2024/10/22/global-financial-stability-report-october-2024","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b336","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-1.4","reading":"CI-1","concept":"AI supervisory evidence","question":"A regulator wants to monitor AI-driven trading risk without treating every model as equally hazardous. Which information request is most useful?","choices":["Inventory material use cases, model ownership, data lineage, external dependencies, validation and escalation controls.","Request only the programming language used by each firm.","Presume an AI label requires banning the model regardless of its role.","Replace model documentation with a statement that AI improves efficiency."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le superviseur doit comprendre la fonction du modèle, sa matérialité et sa gouvernance. La technologie seule ne mesure pas les conséquences financières.","why":["Décrit des preuves utiles à une approche fondée sur les risques.","Le langage ne détermine pas la matérialité.","Une réponse uniforme ignore les usages.","Un bénéfice annoncé ne démontre pas le contrôle."],"cue":"Superviser l’usage, les dépendances et les contrôles.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2024/10/22/global-financial-stability-report-october-2024","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b337","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-1.1","reading":"CI-1","concept":"AI classification versus investment delegation","question":"A fund first uses ML to classify news by issuer, then proposes letting an agent execute and amend positions without human approval. Which distinction matters most for validation?","choices":["Accuracy on issuer labels alone validates position sizing and execution.","Both uses are equivalent because they share the same model vendor.","Manual review is relevant only to whether the model has a graphical interface.","The second use adds delegated decision and execution risk beyond the initial classification task."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le périmètre change d’une aide à la lecture à une décision avec impact de marché. Les limites, validations et autorisations doivent être adaptées.","why":["Une tâche validée ne valide pas toutes les autres.","Le fournisseur commun ne rend pas les fonctions identiques.","Le besoin de contrôle dépend des décisions, pas de l’interface.","Identifie l’extension matérielle de l’usage."],"cue":"Valider à nouveau lorsque le pouvoir délégué change.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2024/10/22/global-financial-stability-report-october-2024","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b338","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-2.1","reading":"CI-2","concept":"AI supply and demand drivers","question":"A bank observes both cheaper accelerator computing and stronger client demand for personalized digital service. In analyzing AI adoption, how should these be classified?","choices":["Both are demand-side changes because computing has a market price.","Computing cost is unrelated to AI adoption unless regulation changes.","Cheaper computing is a supply-side enabler; demand for personalization is a demand-side incentive.","Both are supply-side changes because a bank purchases technology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"La capacité et le coût technologiques modifient l’offre disponible. Les besoins commerciaux et attentes clients poussent la demande d’usages.","why":["Un prix d’intrant affecte le coût de produire le service.","Une baisse de coût peut faciliter l’adoption directement.","Sépare capacité technologique et incitation économique.","La nature de l’achat ne transforme pas la demande client en offre."],"cue":"Offre : capacité; demande : besoin d’usage.","source":"https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/the-financial-stability-implications-of-artificial-intelligence/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b339","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-2.2","reading":"CI-2","concept":"Supervisory anomaly detection","question":"A supervisor deploys ML to prioritize unusual transaction reports for inspection. False positives and missed cases remain possible. Which governance design is most appropriate?","choices":["Assume historical labeling quality has no effect on the system.","Use validated risk-ranking outputs with human investigation, documented thresholds and monitoring for data drift.","Treat every high anomaly score as proof of misconduct.","Delete records not flagged by the model before audit."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Un signal d’anomalie aide à prioriser mais ne constitue pas une conclusion juridique ou économique. La qualité des données et les erreurs doivent être surveillées.","why":["Les cibles historiques influencent l’apprentissage et sa validation.","Maintient la distinction entre signal et preuve.","Un score ne démontre pas l’infraction.","Supprime une information nécessaire pour contrôler les erreurs."],"cue":"Un score de surveillance priorise une enquête.","source":"https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/the-financial-stability-implications-of-artificial-intelligence/","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b340","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-2.3","reading":"CI-2","concept":"Hidden AI vendor common dependency","question":"Three banks contract with different AI providers, but all providers use the same upstream cloud and model host. Which resilience assessment is most informative?","choices":["Map dependencies through subcontractors and test simultaneous loss of the shared upstream service.","Count three contracts as three fully independent operational backups.","Test each provider only during normal operating hours.","Treat vendor diversification as sufficient even without tested exit or fallback arrangements."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Des fournisseurs commerciaux distincts peuvent cacher un même point de défaillance. La cartographie doit traverser les couches de sous-traitance.","why":["Teste la dépendance réelle commune.","Le nombre de contrats ne mesure pas l’indépendance.","Un test partiel peut manquer une indisponibilité commune.","Un recours alternatif doit aussi être opérationnel."],"cue":"Trois fournisseurs peuvent cacher un seul point de panne.","source":"https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/the-financial-stability-implications-of-artificial-intelligence/","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b341","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-2.3","reading":"CI-2","concept":"Self-reinforcing AI credit decisions","question":"Several lenders retrain AI credit models using data affected by their own earlier credit withdrawals. What risk should independent model review investigate?","choices":["More frequent retraining automatically removes endogeneity.","Observed repayment data are independent of access to refinancing by construction.","The only relevant concern is the software license cost.","Feedback can reinforce an initial withdrawal and make the training data reflect model-induced outcomes rather than stable borrower risk alone."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Les décisions changent les situations ensuite observées. Le modèle peut apprendre une boucle qu’il a lui-même contribué à créer.","why":["Une fréquence accrue peut renforcer la boucle.","Le financement influence la capacité de remboursement.","Le coût ne couvre pas le mécanisme de risque décrit.","Identifie l’endogénéité de la donnée et la rétroaction."],"cue":"Les décisions du modèle peuvent changer ses futures données.","source":"https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/the-financial-stability-implications-of-artificial-intelligence/","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b342","topic":"current","skill":"x-ai","objective":"CI-2.3","reading":"CI-2","concept":"Deepfake market misinformation","question":"An apparent central-bank announcement circulates in a synthetic video and several automated systems begin trading. Which response most directly addresses the vulnerability?","choices":["Wait for realized trading profit before checking authenticity.","Conclude the event cannot affect markets if the underlying model code was validated.","Authenticate information against trusted channels and test trading controls for rapidly spreading false signals.","Assume a high-resolution video is stronger evidence than an authenticated official release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le canal est une information trompeuse transmise rapidement. L’authentification et les contrôles d’exécution doivent être testés ensemble.","why":["Le profit n’établit pas la véracité d’un événement.","Un code valide peut réagir à une donnée falsifiée.","Cible origine du signal et transmission aux ordres.","La qualité visuelle ne garantit pas l’authenticité."],"cue":"Vérifier la source avant d’accélérer la réaction.","source":"https://www.fsb.org/2024/11/the-financial-stability-implications-of-artificial-intelligence/","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b343","topic":"current","skill":"x-private","objective":"CI-3.1","reading":"CI-3","concept":"Listed BDC versus loan liquidity","question":"An investor can sell shares of a listed BDC intraday. The BDC holds directly negotiated loans with limited secondary trading. Which statement is best?","choices":["A listed BDC has the same insured-deposit liabilities as a commercial bank.","Share trading provides investor exit through a market price, while underlying loan liquidity and potential share-price discounts remain distinct risks.","Intraday share trading makes every underlying loan intraday-liquid at par.","A shareholder sale necessarily forces the BDC to redeem that investor at NAV."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La liquidité du titre coté n’est pas celle des prêts détenus. La sortie peut se faire à une décote par rapport à la NAV.","why":["Une BDC n’est pas une banque de dépôts.","Distingue liquidité du véhicule et de ses actifs.","Le wrapper coté ne transforme pas les prêts.","Une vente en Bourse n’est pas un rachat direct par le fonds."],"cue":"Une part liquide peut détenir des actifs illiquides.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2503b.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b344","topic":"current","skill":"x-private","objective":"CI-3.2","reading":"CI-3","concept":"Interpreting driver regression","question":"In a hypothetical cross-country regression, private-credit origination is negatively associated with policy rates after included controls. Which conclusion is warranted?","choices":["The estimate supports a conditional association, but causal interpretation still requires addressing identification and omitted variables.","A rate cut is proven to cause the same origination increase in every country.","The coefficient means private-credit borrowers cannot have floating-rate loans.","The result rules out supply-side changes in bank lending."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une association conditionnelle est informative sans démontrer une intervention causale uniforme. Les facteurs omis et la sélection restent à examiner.","why":["Respecte la portée de l’estimation.","Transforme une régression en loi causale universelle.","Le type de taux contractuel ne découle pas de ce signe.","Plusieurs mécanismes peuvent coexister."],"cue":"Coefficient conditionnel ne signifie pas causalité universelle.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2503b.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b345","topic":"current","skill":"x-private","objective":"CI-3.3","reading":"CI-3","concept":"Funding cost convergence decomposition","question":"A private-credit vehicle’s relative cost of capital falls after its required equity return declines and its debt weight rises. What is the best interpretation, holding component debt costs fixed?","choices":["A larger debt weight makes its equity risk disappear.","A lower required equity return is mechanically the same as a lower loan default rate.","Convergence proves private-credit and bank liabilities have identical guarantees.","Both changes can reduce its weighted funding cost, but more leverage can increase risk and alter component costs in practice."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Une pondération plus forte d’une dette moins chère peut réduire le coût moyen, comme une baisse du coût des fonds propres. Le levier ne devient pas gratuit pour autant.","why":["Le levier augmente souvent le risque résiduel de l’equity.","Le rendement exigé dépend de plusieurs risques et prix.","Des coûts proches n’impliquent pas des protections identiques.","Sépare décomposition comptable et risque de levier."],"cue":"Coût moyen plus bas ne signifie pas risque inchangé.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2503b.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b346","topic":"current","skill":"x-private","objective":"CI-3.1","reading":"CI-3","concept":"Fund specialization concentration index","question":"A private-credit fund lends 60% to software and 40% to health services. Using HHI=sum of squared sector weights, its sector concentration index is:","choices":["1.00","0.24","0.52","0.50"],"answer":2,"explanation":"HHI=0,60²+0,40²=0,36+0,16=0,52. Une croissance des secteurs servis au niveau global n’implique pas qu’un fonds individuel soit diversifié.","why":["Indiquerait un seul secteur.","Donne le produit des deux poids sans les carrés.","Additionne les poids sectoriels au carré.","Serait la valeur de deux secteurs à poids égaux."],"cue":"La diversité de l’industrie n’est pas celle du fonds.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2503b.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"0.6**2+0.4**2","value":0.52,"optionValue":0.52,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b347","topic":"current","skill":"x-private","objective":"CI-3.3","reading":"CI-3","concept":"Capital cost calculation for direct lender","question":"A hypothetical lender holds assets of 100, financed by debt of 80 costing 6% and equity of 20 requiring 14%. Ignore taxes, fees and changes in component costs. Its weighted annual funding cost is:","choices":["14.0%","7.6%","6.0%","10.0%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Coût pondéré=0,8×6 %+0,2×14 %=7,6 %. Les poids doivent être mesurés relativement aux actifs financés.","why":["Ignore la dette représentant 80 % du financement.","Pondère dette et equity selon les montants.","Ignore le coût des fonds propres.","Fait une moyenne simple non pondérée."],"cue":"Pondérer les deux coûts, pas seulement la dette.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2503b.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"0.8*6+0.2*14","value":7.6,"optionValue":7.6,"tolerance":0.0001}},{"id":"b348","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.1","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Geopolitical real-financial transmission","question":"A trade restriction blocks a critical imported input used by a bank’s borrowers. The bank has little direct cross-border exposure. Which stress design is best?","choices":["Transmit the input shock into borrower margins, defaults and collateral values, then assess correlated bank losses and available buffers.","Stress only the foreign-exchange desk because the shock originated abroad.","Assign zero loss to all domestic borrowers by domicile.","Increase every foreign sovereign spread equally while leaving corporate cash flows unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un choc géopolitique agit aussi par les chaînes de production et le crédit domestique. Le scénario doit suivre ces liens économiques.","why":["Relie choc réel et effets de bilan.","Le canal ne se limite pas au change.","La domiciliation ne mesure pas les dépendances.","Un choc uniforme manque le mécanisme spécifique."],"cue":"Suivre les flux économiques jusqu’aux bilans.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b349","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.2","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Commodity importer versus exporter","question":"A geopolitical disruption raises the world oil price. Country A imports oil and subsidizes domestic fuel; B exports oil and has no offsetting output disruption. All else equal, which comparison is most plausible?","choices":["Both must receive identical fiscal gains because the oil price is global.","A’s import bill necessarily falls because subsidies fix consumer prices.","B’s export revenue falls solely because the world price rises.","A faces pressure on its external and fiscal balances, while B can receive a terms-of-trade benefit."],"answer":3,"explanation":"L’effet dépend de la position économique. L’importateur subventionnant peut subir facture extérieure et coût budgétaire; l’exportateur peut bénéficier du prix supérieur.","why":["Un prix mondial n’implique pas une exposition identique.","La subvention déplace le coût vers le budget.","À volumes inchangés, un prix supérieur augmente la recette.","Applique les hypothèses distinctes des deux pays."],"cue":"Même choc mondial, expositions locales différentes.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b350","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.3","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Cross-border tariff shock channels","question":"Country A raises tariffs on imports from B. A portfolio manager labels only B-domiciled equities exposed. Which analysis best captures likely cross-border stock effects?","choices":["Assume every A-domiciled company benefits equally from the tariff.","Ignore third countries because they are not named in the policy.","Map sales, production, suppliers and competitors across countries, since A-domiciled importers and third-country substitutes can also be affected.","Classify exposure solely by the exchange on which each stock trades."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les revenus et coûts traversent les frontières. Les tarifs peuvent toucher importateurs, exportateurs et concurrents de substitution, au-delà du domicile.","why":["Les entreprises de A peuvent dépendre des intrants taxés.","Les substitutions commerciales créent des effets indirects.","Relie valorisation et exposition économique réelle.","Le lieu de cotation ne détermine pas les flux."],"cue":"Une carte des revenus vaut mieux qu’un drapeau.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b351","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.4","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Sovereign risk-premium response","question":"After an adverse geopolitical shock, a vulnerable sovereign’s expected tax base weakens and investors demand more compensation for downside fiscal risk. Risk-free rates are unchanged. Which bond effect is most consistent?","choices":["Unchanged risk-free rates imply unchanged sovereign borrowing costs.","Its sovereign spread can widen, reducing the price of outstanding fixed-rate debt.","Its spread must narrow because weaker growth reduces every component of yield.","Outstanding fixed coupons rise immediately to offset the spread."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le rendement souverain comprend une composante de risque propre. Elle peut monter même si le taux sans risque reste stable, faisant baisser le prix d’une obligation fixe.","why":["L’écart souverain fait aussi partie du coût.","Distingue taux de référence et prime souveraine.","La prime de risque peut dominer d’autres effets.","Les coupons contractuels ne se réinitialisent pas."],"cue":"Risque souverain et taux sans risque peuvent diverger.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b352","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.5","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Option-implied geopolitical tail price","question":"Following geopolitical news, deep out-of-the-money equity puts become more expensive relative to at-the-money options, even though spot barely moves. Which inference is most defensible?","choices":["The price of downside insurance has risen, reflecting risk-neutral tail probabilities and/or risk premiums rather than uniquely a physical crash probability.","The physical probability of a crash is uniquely identified by the put price alone.","A stable spot price proves that downside risk pricing is unchanged.","The higher put price necessarily means the issuer’s realized default probability has already increased."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Les options combinent probabilités et prix du risque. Un renchérissement relatif des puts signale un prix accru de protection sans identifier seul une probabilité physique.","why":["Respecte la différence mesure risque-neutre et mesure réelle.","Le prix du risque empêche cette identification simple.","Le spot et la distribution implicite peuvent bouger différemment.","Une option actions ne mesure pas directement un défaut réalisé."],"cue":"Une prime d’assurance n’est pas une probabilité physique.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b353","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.6","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Geopolitical shock and fund flows","question":"An open-end fund owns illiquid corporate debt linked to a sanctioned supply chain. Investors redeem after a geopolitical shock. Which joint stress is most relevant?","choices":["Only a change in the fund’s management fee.","A credit shock with fixed zero redemptions despite the observed withdrawals.","A scenario treating every reported mark as executable for unlimited volume.","Deteriorating issuer cash flows combined with redemptions, costly sales and possible price feedback."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La détérioration fondamentale et les sorties peuvent agir simultanément. Des ventes forcées peuvent alors amplifier les prix et pertes.","why":["Ne couvre pas le choc décrit.","Contredit les flux observés.","Ignore la profondeur de marché.","Combine crédit et liquidité avec leurs interactions."],"cue":"Choc géopolitique : pertes et sorties peuvent se renforcer.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b354","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-4.4","reading":"CI-4","concept":"Sovereign spread duration loss","question":"A sovereign bond has modified duration 5 and price 100. A geopolitical shock widens its spread by 80 basis points; the risk-free curve is unchanged. Ignoring convexity and any cash payment, its approximate new price is:","choices":["99.6","95","96","104"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Variation relative≈−Dmod×Δspread=−5×0,008=−4 %. Nouveau prix≈96. Le spread est converti en décimal.","why":["Traite 80 bps comme 8 bps.","Applique une variation de rendement de 1 %.","Applique la sensibilité avec le signe correct.","Inverse le signe prix-rendement."],"cue":"80 bps = 0,008 en durée.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/GFSR/Issues/2025/04/22/global-financial-stability-report-april-2025","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"100*(1-5*0.008)","value":96,"optionValue":96,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b355","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-5.1","reading":"CI-5","concept":"Conflicting fiscal monetary impulses","question":"Inflation is above target. The central bank raises rates while the government introduces a broad, debt-financed demand stimulus. Which interaction deserves attention?","choices":["Fiscal policy affects only allocation, never aggregate demand.","Fiscal support can offset disinflationary demand restraint and raise the monetary tightening needed, while higher rates worsen fiscal financing pressure.","The two measures necessarily cancel with no effect on debt or inflation.","Higher rates reduce the interest bill on every debt instrument immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Le mélange peut accroître la tension entre stabilisation des prix et financement public. Les effets dépendent aussi de la dette et des horizons.","why":["Dépenses et impôts influencent aussi la demande.","Suit les canaux croisés demande-financement.","Les transmissions et calendriers ne sont pas identiques.","Les refinancements ou taux variables peuvent augmenter les coûts."],"cue":"Analyser le mélange des politiques, pas chaque outil isolé.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/arpdf/ar2023e2.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b356","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-5.2","reading":"CI-5","concept":"Changing signs of policy instability","question":"An analyst argues that low consumer-price inflation proves a long period of monetary and fiscal accommodation stayed safely within the region of stability. What is the strongest qualification?","choices":["Financial imbalances and leverage can accumulate even with low inflation, so instability need not first appear as a price-level acceleration.","Low inflation implies that bank leverage cannot increase.","The stability region depends only on the current inflation number.","Any credit expansion proves that hyperinflation is inevitable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Une économie peut accumuler vulnérabilités financières avant une inflation élevée. Le diagnostic doit inclure bilans, confiance et marge de politique.","why":["Distingue stabilité des prix et stabilité macrofinancière.","Les contraintes de crédit ne sont pas fixées par l’inflation seule.","La région dépend de plusieurs facteurs et de leur évolution.","Le crédit ne conduit pas nécessairement à cet extrême."],"cue":"Inflation calme ne signifie pas bilans solides.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/arpdf/ar2023e2.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b357","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-5.3","reading":"CI-5","concept":"Debt refinancing and interest burden","question":"A sovereign has debt of 200, all initially paying 2% fixed coupons. One quarter of principal refinances this year at 6%; the remaining debt keeps its coupon. Ignore issuance timing, deficits and amortization changes. Annual interest after refinancing is:","choices":["12","4","8","6"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Intérêt=150×2 %+50×6 %=3+3=6. Appliquer 6 % à tout le stock surestime l’effet immédiat de refinancement.","why":["Applique le nouveau taux à toute la dette.","Conserve le taux initial sur toute la dette.","Double l’intérêt initial sans intégrer les bons poids.","Pondère le nouveau taux par la dette refinancée."],"cue":"Le coût réagit au rythme des échéances.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/arpdf/ar2023e2.htm","tier":"coverage","level":3,"numeric":{"expression":"200*0.75*0.02+200*0.25*0.06","value":6,"optionValue":6,"tolerance":0.001}},{"id":"b358","topic":"current","skill":"x-macro","objective":"CI-5.1","reading":"CI-5","concept":"Region of stability uncertainty","question":"Two countries have the same public debt ratio and policy rate but different currency credibility, financing structures and financial leverage. Which assessment best reflects the BIS region-of-stability concept?","choices":["The region is a fixed rectangle unchanged by confidence or financial structure.","The concept prescribes a single inflation rate that eliminates fiscal constraints.","The same policy settings can have different stability implications; the region is state-dependent and cannot be identified by one universal debt-rate threshold.","Equal debt and policy rates establish identical policy space."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Les marges de politique dépendent du contexte institutionnel et financier. Elles peuvent se contracter si la confiance disparaît.","why":["La région change avec les états et vulnérabilités.","La stabilité monétaire ne supprime pas la contrainte budgétaire.","Applique le caractère variable et multidimensionnel de la région.","Les autres différences citées modifient les contraintes."],"cue":"La marge de politique dépend de l’état du système.","source":"https://www.bis.org/publ/arpdf/ar2023e2.htm","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b359","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-6.1","reading":"CI-6","concept":"Unbacked token versus asset claim","question":"Token U has no claim on reserves, issuer assets or redemption proceeds; its value comes from trading demand. Token S promises redemption against an identified reserve pool. Which distinction is most appropriate?","choices":["U’s exchange listing creates a legally enforceable reserve claim.","U is unbacked; S has a different backing and redemption-risk structure that must be evaluated separately.","Both are unbacked solely because they use a blockchain.","A reserve claim makes S equivalent to insured bank deposits in every jurisdiction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La classification dépend des droits et de l’appui économique, pas du seul registre. La promesse de réserve introduit des risques à vérifier.","why":["Une cotation ne crée pas de droit sur une réserve.","Distingue l’absence d’appui et un mécanisme de rachat.","La technologie commune ne définit pas la garantie.","Les protections bancaires ne sont pas automatiques."],"cue":"Classer selon les droits et le soutien économique.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2022/09/26/Regulating-the-Crypto-Ecosystem-The-Case-of-Unbacked-Crypto-Assets-523715","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b360","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-6.2","reading":"CI-6","concept":"Crypto intermediary vertical conflicts","question":"A crypto platform simultaneously runs an exchange, holds client keys and trades for its own account, with no segregation of client assets. Which control package addresses the core risks most directly?","choices":["Client-asset segregation, custody safeguards, conflict controls and risk-based authorization of the functions performed.","Only a faster matching engine.","A disclosure that the platform uses distributed ledgers, without custody controls.","A rule limiting coin logo designs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le cumul des fonctions crée des risques de garde, conflit et usage des actifs clients. Les protections doivent cibler ces fonctions concrètes.","why":["Traite les principaux points de confiance centralisés.","La vitesse ne protège pas les actifs clients.","Un registre distribué n’empêche pas l’abus de garde.","Aucun lien avec les risques financiers du cas."],"cue":"Réguler aussi les intermédiaires, pas seulement les tokens.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2022/09/26/Regulating-the-Crypto-Ecosystem-The-Case-of-Unbacked-Crypto-Assets-523715","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b361","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-6.3","reading":"CI-6","concept":"Risk-based prudential crypto treatment","question":"Considering the approaches discussed in the assigned 2022 IMF note rather than asserting current law, which bank-capital principle is most consistent for highly volatile unbacked crypto exposures?","choices":["Zero capital solely because the asset is digitally recorded.","The same treatment as domestic cash regardless of volatility or legal rights.","No consideration of concentration because positions can be transferred electronically.","A conservative risk-sensitive prudential treatment distinct from automatically treating the token like a conventional low-risk asset."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La prudence doit refléter volatilité, pertes potentielles et caractéristiques de l’actif. La question porte sur une approche de la lecture, pas une règle juridique actuelle.","why":["Le format numérique ne garantit pas la valeur.","Le risque économique diffère de celui du cash.","Une transférabilité technique ne supprime pas la concentration.","Relie exigences et profil de risque."],"cue":"Un traitement prudentiel suit le risque, pas l’étiquette.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2022/09/26/Regulating-the-Crypto-Ecosystem-The-Case-of-Unbacked-Crypto-Assets-523715","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b362","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-6.4","reading":"CI-6","concept":"Country crypto regulatory roadmap","question":"A country following the Bali Fintech Agenda wants to permit useful innovation while limiting crypto risks. Its supervisors lack data and specialist capacity. Which sequence is most defensible?","choices":["Promise that innovation alone resolves consumer and financial-stability risks.","Delay all monitoring until the ecosystem is large enough to create a crisis.","Assess the local ecosystem and risks, clarify legal and regulatory responsibilities, build capacity and coordinate across agencies and borders.","Copy one foreign license label without assessing domestic institutions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Une stratégie adaptée requiert compréhension du marché, capacité et coopération. Le cadre doit soutenir les bénéfices sans laisser les risques hors périmètre.","why":["Les bénéfices n’annulent pas les externalités.","Le suivi précoce aide à construire le dispositif.","Suit une démarche proportionnée et coordonnée.","Une transposition formelle ne garantit pas l’efficacité."],"cue":"Comprendre, délimiter, renforcer et coopérer.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2022/09/26/Regulating-the-Crypto-Ecosystem-The-Case-of-Unbacked-Crypto-Assets-523715","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b363","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-6.2","reading":"CI-6","concept":"Regulatory perimeter by function","question":"A service calls itself a decentralized protocol, but a small company controls access, custody and customer trades. Which supervisory assessment best follows a functional risk-based approach?","choices":["Assume clients hold their own keys because the marketing uses the word protocol.","Examine actual control and services rather than accepting the decentralized label as proof that no intermediary obligations apply.","Exclude the company automatically because the service uses smart contracts.","Assess only whether the token price rose during the last month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Les responsabilités suivent les fonctions réellement exercées. Une appellation technique ne suffit pas à exclure garde ou intermédiation.","why":["Il faut vérifier les pratiques effectives de garde.","Identifie la substance de l’activité et du contrôle.","Le code peut coexister avec des intermédiaires centraux.","La performance récente ne détermine pas le périmètre."],"cue":"Le périmètre suit les fonctions réelles.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2022/09/26/Regulating-the-Crypto-Ecosystem-The-Case-of-Unbacked-Crypto-Assets-523715","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b364","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.1","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Token record versus enforceable right","question":"A ledger records a token as representing ownership of a warehouse, but the applicable property registry does not recognize that transfer. What is the main qualification?","choices":["A shared digital record does not by itself establish enforceable ownership of the underlying asset.","Consensus among validators necessarily overrides property law.","A token identifier guarantees that the asset is unencumbered.","Programmability makes external legal recognition irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Le registre représente une information ou un droit; son lien juridique avec l’actif doit être établi. Le consensus technique ne suffit pas.","why":["Distingue représentation numérique et droit opposable.","Les validateurs ne remplacent pas les autorités compétentes.","Il faut contrôler les sûretés et titres.","Les droits externes conditionnent la valeur économique."],"cue":"Un token doit être relié à un droit opposable.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":3},{"id":"b365","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.2","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Programmable corporate actions and oracles","question":"A tokenized bond automatically changes coupon payments when an external inflation index is published. Which risk remains central despite automation?","choices":["Automation removes the need to verify the inflation input.","A shared ledger guarantees that every external statistic is correct.","The bond no longer exposes its holder to issuer default.","Incorrect or manipulated external data can trigger the wrong contractual payment unless the data source and correction process are governed."],"answer":3,"explanation":"Le code exécute une règle avec des entrées qui peuvent être fausses. La gouvernance de l’oracle et des corrections reste donc importante.","why":["Une exécution correcte peut utiliser une mauvaise donnée.","Le consensus porte sur l’enregistrement, pas toute vérité externe.","L’émetteur doit toujours honorer la créance.","Relie automatisation et dépendance à la donnée."],"cue":"Code correct + donnée fausse = paiement faux possible.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b366","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.3","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Programmable collateral shock propagation","question":"Several tokenized lending arrangements automatically liquidate collateral when a shared price threshold is crossed. Which externality is most important?","choices":["Each contract’s local validity guarantees system-wide stability.","A shared ledger prevents any institution from holding leverage.","Linked automatic liquidations can transmit a shock quickly through prices and contingent contracts.","Atomic execution implies that liquidation has zero market impact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Des règles individuellement cohérentes peuvent déclencher des ventes communes. La programmabilité accélère alors une transmission de prix et de garanties.","why":["Le résultat collectif dépend des interactions.","Un registre n’interdit pas le financement à levier.","Teste la chaîne d’externalités et d’exécution.","L’atomicité ne supprime pas la profondeur limitée."],"cue":"Des contrats corrects peuvent former une boucle fragile.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b367","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.4","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Broker competition versus infrastructure concentration","question":"Tokenization lowers entry costs for retail brokers, but most users migrate to one shared ledger because it has the largest network. What market-structure result is plausible?","choices":["Retail access removes the need for custody and investor protection.","Broker competition can increase while core infrastructure becomes more concentrated.","Lower broker entry costs guarantee decentralization of every infrastructure layer.","A dominant ledger eliminates switching and interoperability concerns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"La concurrence sur un service et la concentration de son infrastructure peuvent évoluer en sens opposés. Les effets de réseau favorisent parfois un point central.","why":["Les fonctions de garde et les droits restent essentiels.","Distingue deux niveaux de structure de marché.","La concurrence aval ne garantit pas la dispersion amont.","La domination peut accroître ces dépendances."],"cue":"Plus de courtiers peut coexister avec un registre dominant.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b368","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.5","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Trust in permissioned consensus","question":"A consortium ledger restricts validation to five approved institutions. Three can jointly approve invalid transfers under its consensus rules. Which trust assessment is most appropriate?","choices":["Permissioned access changes the trust model but does not remove governance, collusion and validator-security risks.","Approved validators cannot collude by definition.","A permissioned ledger requires no operational controls.","The ledger has the same failure assumptions as every permissionless proof-of-work chain."],"answer":0,"explanation":"La restriction d’accès identifie les acteurs de confiance mais ne prouve pas leur honnêteté ou leur sécurité. Il faut analyser le seuil et la gouvernance.","why":["Évalue les hypothèses concrètes de validation.","L’approbation n’est pas une garantie absolue.","Les identités connues ne suppriment pas les pannes.","Les mécanismes et incitations peuvent être différents."],"cue":"Confiance permissionnée : vérifier qui peut agir et à quel seuil.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b369","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-7.2","reading":"CI-7","concept":"Instant gross settlement funding tradeoff","question":"A tokenized settlement design replaces end-of-day netting with prefunded instantaneous gross settlement. Counterparty principal risk falls. What tradeoff still needs analysis?","choices":["Every reduction in counterparty risk necessarily reduces liquidity needs to zero.","Instant settlement makes the payment asset risk-free.","Removing netting guarantees lower total funding for all participants.","More intraday liquidity may be required because offsetting obligations are no longer netted before funding."],"answer":3,"explanation":"La réduction du risque de contrepartie peut s’accompagner d’un besoin accru de préfinancement. Les gains dépendent du calendrier et des possibilités de compensation.","why":["Un risque réduit peut déplacer la contrainte vers le cash.","Le moyen de paiement conserve son propre risque.","La compensation peut justement économiser du financement.","Identifie le coût de liquidité d’un règlement brut préfinancé."],"cue":"Gagner en règlement peut coûter en préfinancement.","source":"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/fintech-notes/Issues/2025/01/29/Tokenization-and-Financial-Market-Inefficiencies-561256","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b370","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-8.1","reading":"CI-8","concept":"Adversarial cyber risk modeling","question":"A bank models cyber losses only from a stationary sample of past incidents. Its systems and attacker techniques change rapidly. Which concern is most important?","choices":["A year without a breach proves the annual attack probability is zero.","Operational changes cannot alter the loss distribution once a model is fitted.","Adaptive adversaries, changing dependencies and sparse incident data can make historical frequency estimates unstable.","Cyber events are identical to interest-rate shocks because both produce money losses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Le risque cyber dépend d’adversaires adaptatifs et d’une architecture changeante. Une fréquence historique stable peut être une hypothèse trop forte.","why":["L’absence d’événement ne prouve pas une probabilité nulle.","Les changements de système peuvent modifier exposition et sévérité.","Conteste la stabilité statistique avec les mécanismes pertinents.","La conséquence monétaire commune n’unifie pas les mécanismes."],"cue":"Un adversaire apprend et le système change.","source":"https://www.bde.es/f/webbde/GAP/Secciones/Publicaciones/InformesBoletinesRevistas/RevistaEstabilidadFinanciera/22/3_FSR43_Digital.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b371","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-8.2","reading":"CI-8","concept":"Data integrity and financial contagion","question":"A cyberattack corrupts position records at a major settlement intermediary. Participants cannot verify exposures and withhold payments, although their assets are solvent. Which transmission is most relevant?","choices":["Only direct theft of money can create systemic cyber risk.","An integrity and operational shock can become a liquidity and confidence shock across connected institutions.","The event is purely an accounting issue until a borrower defaults.","Solvency guarantees that all payments continue on time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"L’incertitude sur les positions et le blocage des flux peuvent créer un manque de liquidité et une perte de confiance indépendamment d’un défaut initial.","why":["Une corruption de données peut suffire à désorganiser le réseau.","Suit le passage opérationnel vers la contagion financière.","L’interruption des paiements a déjà un effet économique.","Des établissements solvables peuvent manquer de liquidité."],"cue":"Intégrité des données → confiance → liquidité.","source":"https://www.bde.es/f/webbde/GAP/Secciones/Publicaciones/InformesBoletinesRevistas/RevistaEstabilidadFinanciera/22/3_FSR43_Digital.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":4},{"id":"b372","topic":"current","skill":"x-digital","objective":"CI-8.3","reading":"CI-8","concept":"Collective IT buffer design","question":"Authorities propose a shared emergency processing facility for several banks. Which design review most directly addresses the risk that the buffer fails during a common outage?","choices":["Test independent technology and data recovery, joint capacity and coordinated access rules under simultaneous demand.","Place the buffer on exactly the same untested critical stack and assume geographical distance is sufficient.","Test each bank in isolation with no other users of the backup.","Treat additional bank capital as a complete substitute for restoring processing capability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Un dispositif collectif doit rester disponible face au choc commun et à une demande simultanée. La capacité et les règles d’accès font partie du test.","why":["Teste indépendance et fonctionnement collectif.","Une dépendance logicielle commune peut survivre à la distance.","Ne teste pas la concurrence pour la capacité partagée.","Le capital absorbe des pertes sans réparer un système indisponible."],"cue":"Le backup doit survivre au choc commun et à l’usage commun.","source":"https://www.bde.es/f/webbde/GAP/Secciones/Publicaciones/InformesBoletinesRevistas/RevistaEstabilidadFinanciera/22/3_FSR43_Digital.pdf","tier":"coverage","level":4}];
